/* 段落记忆 · 词层 2 · 子块 b：词头 → {tw:[关系词,关系类型], en, zh} */
window.APP_MERGE_NET(2,{"sub":"b","par":{"gather":{"tw":[["meet",3],["pick",3],["collect",0],["pull",2],["club",3],["spread",1],["gain",0],["prepare",6]],"en":"Every autumn the neighbours gather in the old apple garden. We meet at eight, when the grass is still wet, and begin to pick the fruit. My job is to collect the full boxes and pull them to the road. The reading club sends four helpers, and together we spread a long cloth under the biggest tree. During the break we sit on the cloth and gain new friends over tea. Some children come with small baskets and stay until the sun is high. Nobody talks about money here; we only prepare the pies and share them out.","zh":"每年秋天邻居们都会聚到那片老苹果园里。我们八点碰头，草还湿着，就开始摘果子。我的活是把装满的箱子收起来、拖到路边。读书会派来四个帮手，我们一起在最大的那棵树下铺开一大块布。休息时大家坐在布上喝茶，还认识了不少新朋友。这里没人谈钱，我们只准备馅饼，然后分着吃。"},"increase":{"tw":[["rate",6],["increment",0],["grow",3],["add",3],["reduce",6],["decrease",1],["process",2],["gain",0]],"en":"Last year the price of bread began to increase. In the same month the rate for bus tickets went up too. A small increment to a city budget may not look like much, but families feel it at the end of the week. Some people decided to grow their own vegetables, and the garden shops began to add new customers. The city tried to reduce the cost of school meals, which made the total decrease a little. It is a slow process, and everyone hopes to gain something from the change.","zh":"去年面包的价格开始上涨。同一个月，公交车票的费率也涨了。城市预算上小幅度的一增看着不多，但家庭到周末就能感觉到。有人决定自己种菜，园艺店于是多了些新顾客。市里试着压低学校午餐的成本，总额这才降了一点。这是个缓慢的过程，大家都希望从这场变化里得到点什么。"},"divide":{"tw":[["division",4],["line",2],["chip",3],["break",3],["fraction",0],["separate",0],["change",2],["unite",1]],"en":"The old classroom was too small for two groups, so the teacher decided to divide the space with a thin wall. The division was simple: a new line of glass and wood down the middle. One class could not see the other, but the sound still moved through. A few chips of paint fell when the workers broke the old board, and a fraction of the floor stayed wet for a day. Later the students had to separate their desks into two piles. Nothing else had to change. In spring the two classes unite again and open the wall for a school play.","zh":"那间旧教室太小，装不下两个班，老师决定用一道薄墙把空间分开。分法很简单：中间加一道玻璃和木头的隔断线。一个班看不见另一个班，但声音还是能穿过来。工人拆旧木板时掉下几片油漆屑，有一小块地板湿了一整天。后来学生们只好把课桌分成两堆。别的都不用改。到了春天，两个班又重新合并，把墙打开，演一场校园剧。"},"improve":{"tw":[["build",3],["help",3],["amend",0],["ameliorate",0],["change",2],["enhance",6],["better",0],["develop",6]],"en":"Three years ago the river was dirty. The city wanted to improve the water quality before the summer. First it had to build a new pipe under the road, which would help the small factories send clean water back. Then the council worked to amend the old rules, because nobody could ameliorate the problem with paper alone. A group of students began to measure the fish every month. Slowly the colour of the river began to change, and the number of birds grew. It was hard to enhance the result faster, but the water was better than before, and the plan will develop over five years.","zh":"三年前这条河很脏。市里想在夏天之前把水质改善好。先得在路下铺一条新管道，让那些小厂把干净的水送回来。接着市政会又着手修订旧规，因为光靠文件谁也缓解不了这个问题。一群学生开始每月数鱼。河水的颜色慢慢变了，鸟也多了起来。想更快地提升效果很难，但水比从前好了，而这个方案还要做五年。"},"extend":{"tw":[["extension",4],["carry",0],["cross",3],["allow",6],["extensive",4],["continue",2],["spread",3],["return",6],["extent",4]],"en":"The council wanted to extend the old road past the woods, and the plan was extensive. The new extension would cross the small river and spread across two fields. No one could say to what extent the traffic would grow. My neighbour said the noise would carry for miles at night. The farmers asked the council not to allow the work in spring, when the birds return. The men agreed to continue only after the harvest. In the end the road grew by a short stretch, and that was enough. It was not the wide new road the council had promised, but it was something.","zh":"议会想把那条老路一直修过树林，规划铺得很大。新的延伸段要横穿那条小河，还要铺满两片田地。谁也说不清车流会涨到什么程度。我邻居说，夜里噪音能传出好几里。农民们请求议会别在春天动工，那时鸟正回来。工人们答应等收完庄稼再继续。最后这条路只多延了一小段，也就够了。这不是议会当初许下的那条宽阔新路，可总算修了点东西。"},"fail":{"tw":[["failure",4],["break",0],["fall",3],["change",2],["manage",1],["agree",6],["die",0],["miss",3],["disappoint",2],["need",6],["bomb",0]],"en":"The small theatre had one last show, and everyone feared it would fail. The lead actor forgot a line, the lights broke, and the whole thing seemed ready to fall apart. The change of scene took too long, and the audience began to talk. My aunt had to manage the stage alone. She did not agree with the director, who had said the play might bomb, but she would not miss her cue. Yet at the end the laughter died, and the failure hurt more than any of us had need to admit. The empty seats disappointed everyone who had worked on the play for months. She stood alone in the dark and waited.","zh":"小剧场还剩最后一场戏，人人都担心它会砸锅。主角忘了一句词，灯也坏了，整出戏眼看就要散架。换场景拖得太久，观众开始交头接耳。我姑妈只得一个人撑着舞台。导演说过这戏也许会彻底失败，她不认同，可她的出场提示一次也不肯错过。可到最后，笑声还是断了，那份失败带来的难受，比我们谁愿意承认的都要重。空着的座位让每个为这出戏忙了几个月的人都失望了。她一个人站在暗处，等着。"},"float":{"tw":[["flotation",4],["blow",0],["chip",3],["drink",2],["sink",1],["sail",6],["swim",0],["ride",3],["test",2],["hang",6],["drift",3]],"en":"The old wooden boat could still float, though the paint had begun to chip along the side. We took it out on the lake to test the new sail. My brother was hanging it up in the shed when I called him. He ran down and we pushed off. A soft wind began to blow, and the boat started to drift away from the shore. Two boys were swimming near the boat and climbed aboard for a ride. One of them tried to drink from a bottle and nearly made us all fall in. My father said we needed a flotation ring, or the next trip might end in a slow sink.","zh":"那条旧木船还能浮着，尽管船边的漆已经开始一块块掉了。我们把它划到湖上，试那张新帆。我叫我哥的时候，他正在棚里把帆挂起来。他跑下来，我们撑篙离了岸。一阵轻风起了，小船开始朝离岸的方向漂去。两个男孩在船边游水，爬上来搭了个顺风船。其中一个想对着瓶子喝水，差点把我们都弄进湖里。我爸说我们得配个救生圈，不然下一趟可能就慢慢沉下去了。"},"habit":{"tw":[["habitual",4],["use",0],["ritual",3],["dress",2],["penchant",6],["habituate",4],["wont",0],["custom",2],["drink",6]],"en":"My grandfather had a habit of walking to the river before breakfast, and it had become a kind of ritual. He would dress in the same grey coat, take his cup, and drink his tea standing at the door. It was his custom to say nothing until the sun was up. As a young man he had a penchant for talking too much, but he had learned to habituate himself to silence. That was his habitual mood now. He said he had grown used to it, and it was not, as was his wont, a thing to explain. The river never asked him for more.","zh":"我爷爷有个习惯，早饭前总要走到河边去，这已经成了一种仪式。他会穿上那件灰大衣，端起杯子，站在门口把茶喝了。太阳没升起来之前他不说话，这是他的老例。年轻时他偏爱多嘴，后来学会了让自己习惯沉默。如今他惯常就是这个神情。他说他早就习惯了，而按他的老脾气，这事也没什么可解释的。那条河从没向他多要过什么。"},"effect":{"tw":[["effective",4],["force",0],["carry",3],["act",2],["impact",6],["issue",0],["change",3],["cause",2],["due",6],["event",0]],"en":"The heavy rain had a strange effect on the little river. The force of the water carved a new path through the field, and the impact could be seen for weeks. No one knew the exact cause, but the effect was clear. The change came so slowly that people thought it was simply due to the season. My teacher said the storm was one event, not the whole issue. A new wall of stones proved more effective than sand. We watched the river carry the mud away and tried to act as if nothing had happened. It worked better than anyone expected.","zh":"那场大雨给这条小河带来了奇怪的影响。水流的力气在田里冲出一条新道，造成的冲击好几周都看得出来。没人知道确切的原因，但结果很清楚。变化来得太慢，人们只以为是季节的缘故。老师说，那场暴雨只是一件事，并不是问题的全部。新砌的一道石墙，比沙子顶用多了。我们看着河水把泥冲走，尽量装作什么都没发生。它起的作用比谁预想的都好。"},"equal":{"tw":[["equate",4],["touch",0],["tie",3],["change",2],["differ",1],["individual",6],["match",3],["associate",3],["respect",6],["adequate",0]],"en":"In our class no two students were ever truly equal, though the teacher wanted us to see each one as an individual. She would never equate a quick answer with a good mind. When two teams played a match, the score might tie, but the players still differ in skill. We were told to respect the other side and to touch hands at the end. A slow reader next to me said the change in her marks was small but real, and that it was adequate for her. I began to associate her name with quiet courage. That was enough for me to remember.","zh":"我们班里从来没有两个学生真的一模一样，可老师希望我们每个人都被当成独立的一个人看。她从不会把一个快答等同于一个好脑子。两支队伍打比赛，比分可能打平，可选手的本事还是各有不同。我们被要求尊重对手，结束时互相碰一下手。坐在我旁边一个读得慢的同学说，她分数上的变化不大，却是真的，对她来说也够了。我开始把她的名字和一种安静的勇气连在一起。这足够让我记住她了。"},"flash":{"tw":[["flashy",4],["cheap",0],["flicker",3],["appear",2],["wave",6],["loud",0],["gleam",3],["cover",2],["memory",6],["shoot",0]],"en":"Late at night a bright flash lit the window of the small hotel, and for a moment everything seemed cheap and flashy. A light began to flicker on the wall, then a tall shape appeared in the doorway. Someone shouted a loud word from the street below. I saw a gleam of metal, and a wave of fear went through me. My only memory of that hour is the way the lamp seemed to cover the room in white. I tried to shoot a picture with my phone, but the light was gone before I could. I never told anyone what happened.","zh":"深夜，一道亮光闪过那家小旅馆的窗户，一时间一切都显得廉价又花哨。墙上的一盏灯开始忽明忽暗，接着门口出现一个高高的身影。楼下街上有人喊了一句很响的话。我瞥见一点金属的光，一阵恐惧窜过全身。那一个小时我唯一记得的，就是那盏灯好像把整间屋子都罩成了白色。我想用手机拍张照，可还没等我按下，光就没了。那晚的事，我从没跟人提过。"},"fold":{"tw":[["folder",4],["close",0],["cross",3],["change",2],["divide",6],["bend",0],["collapse",3],["pen",2],["wrap",6],["flock",3]],"en":"On the kitchen table my mother would fold each letter twice and set it in a grey folder. She would close the old road map, cross out the wrong names, and write a short note with her pen. When a plan had to change, she would bend it like paper until it fit. One pile could divide into three: to keep, to answer, to throw away. She said a loose stack would collapse if we let it grow. Then she would wrap the whole bundle in string, and the flock of small papers would finally become one neat parcel. It was a small ritual of hers.","zh":"在厨房桌上，我妈会把每封信折两下，放进一个灰文件夹里。她会合上那张旧路线图，划掉写错的名字，用笔写上一句短话。计划要是有变，她会像折纸一样把它弯一弯，直到合适为止。一摞东西可以分成三堆：留着的、要回信的、扔掉的。她说这一沓要是放任它堆下去，迟早会塌。然后她会用绳子把整捆扎好，那一群零散纸片终于变成一个整整齐齐的包裹。这是她的一个小仪式。"},"grace":{"tw":[["gracious",4],["deck",3],["hang",3],["change",2],["joy",6],["ornament",3],["stick",3],["state",2],["love",6],["adorn",0]],"en":"At the small wedding by the river, my aunt moved through the crowd with quiet grace. She was gracious to every guest, even the ones she had never met. Long strings of lights were hanging along the deck, and a paper ornament swayed above each table. Someone had stuck a white flower in her hair. The change in her face was plain to see: pure joy. She said she was in a happy state, and that she still felt the same love she had felt years ago. It was love, she said, that had adorned the whole evening, and no one wanted to leave.","zh":"在河边那场小小的婚礼上，我姑妈带着一种安静的风度在人群里走动。她对每位来客都很亲切，连没见过面的也一样。长廊上挂着一串串灯，每张桌子上方都晃着一件纸做的饰物。有人在她头发上别了一朵白花。她脸上那种变化一眼就看得出来：纯粹的欢喜。她说自己正处在一种快乐的状态里，多年前的那份爱如今还是一样的。她说，正是爱装点了整个晚上，谁都不舍得走。"},"grade":{"tw":[["gradual",4],["class",0],["high",3],["measure",2],["school",6],["course",0],["property",2],["low",3],["intermediate",6],["degree",0]],"en":"My brother moved up a grade last year, and the change was gradual. In his new class the work was harder, and the school set a high standard for every course. The teacher would measure each pupil's progress with a short test. His marks were low at first, then climbed to an intermediate level. He learned about the property of metals and earned a small degree of praise from the head. He said the climb was slow but steady, and he was proud of it. At night he would read the whole chapter again, and in the morning he asked questions.","zh":"我弟弟去年升了一个年级，这变化是慢慢来的。新班级里功课更难，学校对每一门课都定下很高的标准。老师会用一场小测验来衡量每个学生的进步。他的分起初很低，后来爬到了中等水平。他学了金属的特性，还从校长那里得到一点点称赞。他说这一路爬得慢，可很稳，他为此骄傲。晚上他会把整章再读一遍，第二天早上就来问问题。"},"guarantee":{"tw":[["guarantor",4],["insure",0],["cover",3],["back",2],["accept",6],["secure",3],["deposit",3],["promise",2],["maintain",6],["assure",0]],"en":"When my father bought the second-hand van, the seller could not guarantee that the engine would last. He did agree to insure it for a year, and he said his brother would act as guarantor. The deposit was small, and the rest we had to pay in spring. My father wanted to secure a good price and to maintain the old engine himself. He would not accept the first offer. I had to assure him that the brakes were fine and that the papers would cover everything. He made the seller promise to call if anything went wrong, and we drove back slowly.","zh":"我爸买那辆二手面包车时，卖家没法保证发动机能用多久。他答应给它保一年的险，还说让他弟弟做担保人。定金不多，剩下的钱春天再付。我爸想拿到一个好价钱，还打算自己保养那台老发动机。对方第一个报价他不肯接受。我只好向他保证刹车没问题，手续也能把一切都涵盖进去。他让卖家答应出问题就打电话，然后我们慢慢开了回去。"},"hook":{"tw":[["draw",0],["seize",3],["catch",2],["ball",6],["lift",0],["anchor",3],["hit",2],["mouth",6],["cop",0]],"en":"By the harbour wall an old man showed me how to hook a fish. He would draw the line slowly, then seize the rod and catch whatever came up. A heavy ball of rope lay at his feet, and he used it to lift the small anchor. Once a fish hit the hook so hard that it slipped from its mouth. A cop on the corner stopped and watched for a while. The man laughed and said that a good hook was worth more than luck. Then he dropped the line back into the grey water. It was a quiet morning on the quay.","zh":"在港口的墙边，一位老人教我怎么钓鱼上钩。他会慢慢收线，然后一把抓住鱼竿，把上来的东西接住。他脚边放着一团沉甸甸的绳子，用它把小锚提起来。有一次一条鱼撞上钩太猛，从嘴里滑脱了。拐角上一个警察停下来看了一会儿。老人笑着说，一只好钩比运气值钱。然后他把线又丢回灰蒙蒙的水里。码头上的这个早上很安静。"},"identify":{"tw":[["identity",4],["discover",0],["mistake",3],["see",2],["locate",6],["key",0],["taste",3],["associate",2],["specific",6],["distinguish",0]],"en":"The police had to identify the man who left the building that night, but no witness could say a specific name. One neighbour said she could see his face clearly and would not mistake it again. They tried to locate the car by its plate and used a key left in the door. The officer said the taste of the coffee in the cup helped them discover how long the man had waited. Slowly a picture of his identity began to appear. People began to associate the address with the case, and it was hard to distinguish the truth from the talk in the street.","zh":"警方得查明那晚离开大楼的那个男人是谁，可没有目击者说得出一个具体的名字。一位邻居说她能看清他的脸，再不会认错。他们想按车牌找到那辆车，还用了一把留在门上的钥匙。警官说，杯子里咖啡的味道帮他们查出了那男人等了多久。他的身份慢慢有了轮廓。人们开始把这个地址和这桩案子联系起来，街头上的话和真相也越来越难分辨。"},"impress":{"tw":[["impression",4],["move",0],["letter",3],["write",2],["convince",6],["strike",0],["surprise",3],["dye",2],["entertain",6],["affect",2]],"en":"The new machine did not impress me at first, and my first impression was that it was heavy and slow. I had to write a short letter to the maker and move the whole thing into the corner. The colour they used to dye the cover was dull. Still, I had to admit the speed did surprise me, and it could entertain a room full of children for hours. I tried to convince my sister that it was worth the price. Something about its design did strike a note with her, and the idea began to affect my own view as well.","zh":"这台新机器起初并没让我觉得了不起，我的第一印象是它又重又慢。我只得给厂家写了一封短信，把整台机器挪到角落里。他们给外壳染的颜色发闷。可我还是得承认，它的速度确实让我吃了一惊，而且能让一屋子孩子乐上好几个钟头。我试着说服我妹妹它值这个价。它设计上有什么东西确实打动了她，这个念头也开始影响了我的看法。"},"flight":{"tw":[["flee",4],["escape",0],["break",3],["fly",2],["plane",6],["fledge",0],["pass",3],["shoot",2],["aboard",6]],"en":"Our flight was called early, so we had to hurry aboard the plane. My mother said she wanted to fly once more before the year ended. She watched a young bird fledge from a nest near the gate and then shoot into the sky. A worried man tried to flee the crowd, as if he meant to escape the whole airport. Something seemed about to break inside him. We had to pass three checks before we reached our seats. In the end the plane rose late but safely, and my mother slept the whole way. It had been a long day of waiting.","zh":"我们的航班很早就开始登机了，我们只得赶紧上了飞机。我妈说，她想在年底前再飞一次。她看着一只小鸟从门边的窝里长出羽翼，然后一冲飞上天。一个神色不安的男人想挤出人群，好像要逃出整个机场。他心里有什么好像快要断了。我们过了三道检查才走到座位。最后飞机晚点起飞，却平安无事，我妈一路都睡着。这一天等得够久了。"},"intent":{"tw":[["intend",4],["design",0],["mind",3],["goal",2],["justify",6],["purpose",0],["view",3],["legitimate",6],["spirit",0]],"en":"My uncle drew a careful design for a new wooden chair, and his intent was to make it last a lifetime. He would intend every joint to hold without glue. His goal was simple, and he could not justify any shortcut in the purpose of good work. In his view, a chair was a small honest thing. There was one legitimate question, though: would the wood bend with the weather? He kept that worry in the back of his mind. Then he picked up his tools again, and his tired spirit came back to life. The old room smelled of wood and sawdust.","zh":"我叔为一把新木椅细细地画了张设计图，他的用意是让它能用一辈子。他要求每个榫头不靠胶也咬得住。他的目标很简单，在把活干好这件事上，他没法给自己找任何捷径。在他看来，一把椅子就是一件老实的小东西。不过有一个正当的疑问：木头会不会随天气变形？他把这份担心搁在心底。随后他又拿起工具，疲乏的精神也回来了。那间老屋满是木头和锯末的气味。"},"demand":{"tw":[["ask",3],["call",3],["supply",1],["claim",2],["increase",6],["exact",0],["cost",3],["condition",2],["boost",6],["need",0]],"en":"After the first cold week there was a sudden demand for warm blankets, and the little shop could not meet it. The owner had to ask his supplier for a bigger supply and to increase his order by half. He would call a fair price, though the exact cost was still unknown. A woman came in and made a claim about a broken zip, so he gave her one on the condition that she bring the receipt later. This did seem to boost his trade for a while. He said he only ever stocked what people truly need. It was a good week.","zh":"头一个星期冷下来，保暖毯子突然抢手，小店根本供不上。老板只得向供货商要多一些货，把订单加了一半。他会报一个公道的价，尽管确切成本还不知道。一位女士进来，说一条拉链是坏的，他就先给了她一条，条件是她回头把收据拿来。这倒像是让生意旺了一阵。他说他只进人们真正需要的东西。这一周过得不错。"},"direct":{"tw":[["address",3],["blow",3],["control",2],["indirect",1],["possible",6],["head",0],["charge",3],["manage",2],["further",6],["lead",0]],"en":"The head of the office would direct every meeting in a calm, clear way. She gave her address at the door and asked us to control our talk so that others could speak. Her style was direct but never rude, and she hated an indirect answer. A hard blow to the project came when the money ran out, and she had to manage the team alone. She was in charge of the schedule and would not let it slip further. It was not possible to lead without making enemies, she said. Then she asked for one more week. We gave it to her.","zh":"办公室的负责人主持会议总是平静而清楚。她在门口讲了几句话，让我们管住自己的嘴，好让别人也能开口。她的作风直来直去，却从不粗鲁，最讨厌拐弯抹角的答复。钱用光的那天，项目挨了重重一击，她只得一个人把队伍撑起来。进度归她管，她不肯让它再拖下去。她说，当头儿而不树敌是不可能的。然后她要再给一周时间。我们就给了她。"},"engage":{"tw":[["employ",0],["close",3],["act",2],["disengage",1],["pursue",6],["lock",3],["fill",3],["interest",2],["refrain",6],["rent",0]],"en":"The firm wanted to employ one more driver, so they decided to engage a young man from the next town. He had to fill in a long form, and the office would lock the file away at night. His main interest was the old buses, and he hoped to pursue that work for years. The manager told him to act carefully and to refrain from arguing with passengers. If he had to disengage from a difficult talk, he should simply close the door and walk away. The rent on his room was cheap, which helped him accept the offer. It was a good start.","zh":"这家公司想再雇一名司机，于是决定从邻镇请一个年轻人。他得填一张长长的表，办公室夜里会把档案锁起来。他最感兴趣的是那些老式公交车，盼着这活儿能一直干下去。经理叫他做事仔细些，别跟乘客争。要是不得不从一场难缠的谈话里抽身，他索性把门一关走开就好。他租的房子便宜，这也帮着他应下了这份差事。这是个不错的开头。"},"gain":{"tw":[["clear",0],["find",3],["advantage",2],["loss",1],["share",6],["hit",0],["ground",3],["increase",2],["interest",6],["reach",0]],"en":"After a poor year the farm began to gain again, and my uncle could find a clear reason for it. The new well gave him an advantage over the farms that had none, and he was glad to share the water with them. The loss of two cows in spring had hit him hard, but the ground was rich and the crops came back. He saw a small increase in the price of grain, and the interest from the bank was lower than before. By autumn he had reached a steady gain. He did not smile, but he slept better. That was enough for him.","zh":"熬过一个歉收的年份后，农场又开始有了起色，我叔能说出一条清楚的原因。新打的井让他比那些没井的农场占了便宜，他也乐意跟大家分水。春天死了两头牛，打击不轻，可地力好，庄稼又回来了。他看到粮价小涨了一点，银行的利息也比从前低了。到秋天，他挣到了一份稳稳的收益。他没笑，可睡得更香了。对他来说，这就够了。"},"hire":{"tw":[["employ",0],["fill",3],["act",2],["fire",1],["recruit",6],["rent",0],["ship",3],["contract",2],["advise",6],["engage",3]],"en":"The warehouse had to hire two more hands before the busy season began. The manager would employ anyone who could act quickly and fill a heavy order without help. He had to fire one man last month, and now he needed to recruit a replacement. He would rent a third truck and ship the goods out by Friday. Every worker signed a short contract before the first shift. He asked me to advise him on the new crew, and I said he should engage people who lived nearby. In the end six people came for one job. It was a hard week.","zh":"旺季开始前，仓库还得再雇两名帮手。经理愿意用什么人，只要动作快、不用人搭手就能装满一车货。上个月他不得不辞掉一个人，现在得再招一个补上。他打算再租一辆卡车，周五前把货发出去。每个工人上第一个班之前都签一份短合同。他让我给他出主意挑这批新人，我说最好找住得近的。到头来，一个岗位来了六个人应聘。这一周够呛。"},"include":{"tw":[["inclusion",4],["admit",0],["carry",3],["add",2],["exclude",1],["inclusive",4],["count",3]],"en":"The tour price would include the bus, the guide, and one hot meal each day. The small print said the price did not admit anyone under ten, which seemed unfair. We had to carry our own bags, but a kind driver would add a stop for tea. The company could exclude a traveller who broke the rules, and the clerk made us count our tickets twice. She promised a full inclusion of all local fees, and the whole offer was called inclusive. In the end the trip cost more than we had planned. Nobody on the bus complained about it.","zh":"这个团费包含大巴、导游，每天还有一顿热饭。小字里写着不满十岁不能参加，这看着不太公道。行李得自己拎，不过好心的司机答应多加一个喝茶的点。谁要是坏了规矩，公司可以不让他参加，办事员还让我们把票数了两遍。她保证把当地所有费用都算进去，整个报价说是一价全包。到头来，这趟旅行花的钱比我们计划的还多。车上没人为此抱怨。"},"decision":{"tw":[["decide",4],["call",3],["choice",2],["indecision",1],["step",6],["move",3],["result",2],["request",6]],"en":"The manager had to make a hard decision before the shop opened that morning. His indecision had already cost the team a week. He would call the head office and ask for their choice, but in the end he had to decide alone. Every step he took seemed to bring a new request from the staff. One wrong move could change the result of the whole season. He stood by the window and said nothing. Then he wrote his decision on a card and pinned it to the board. Nobody in the room argued with him that day. The shop opened on time.","zh":"那天早上开店之前，经理得做一个艰难的决定。他的犹豫已经让团队耽误了一个星期。他本想打电话问总部要个说法，可到头来还是得自己拿主意。他每走一步，好像都招来员工一个新的要求。一步走错，整个季度的结果就可能不一样。他站在窗边，什么也没说。然后他把决定写在一张卡片上，钉到板子上。那天屋里没人跟他争。店按时开了门。"},"engineer":{"tw":[["engine",4],["direct",0],["choreograph",3],["plan",2],["mechanic",6],["organize",0],["design",2],["pioneer",6]],"en":"The young engineer had to design a new part for the old engine, and he had to plan every step himself. A mechanic from the next town helped him organize the tools. He would direct the whole job as if he were on a stage, and in a way he did choreograph each move of the crew. Some of the older men called him a pioneer, though he laughed at that. In the end the engine started on the first try. He said the work had been simple, but I knew it was not. He stood there, quietly proud of it.","zh":"这位年轻的工程师得给那台老发动机设计一个新零件，每一步都得他自己盘算。邻镇来的一位机械师帮他张罗工具。他像在台上那样调度整个活计，可以说，他把众人每一步动作都编排好了。有些老工人叫他开路人，他听了只是笑笑。最后发动机第一次就着了。他说这活不难，可我知道不是。他站在那儿，心里悄悄地得意。"},"giant":{"tw":[["gigantic",4],["monster",0],["animal",2],["conglomerate",6],["whale",0],["star",2],["venture",6],["titan",0]],"en":"My little brother built a giant snowman in the front yard, and it looked almost gigantic from the road. He called it a monster and gave it two stones for eyes. Our old cat walked past it like a brave little animal. He said it was as big as a whale, and as tall as a star in the sky. Then he told me about a business he wanted to start one day, a small venture that might grow into a conglomerate. He said he would be a titan of the trade. I did not laugh. It was a good snowman.","zh":"我弟弟在前院堆了个大雪人，从路上看过去几乎大得吓人。他管它叫怪物，还给它安了两颗石子当眼睛。我们家那只老猫像只勇敢的小动物似的从它旁边走过。他说它跟鲸鱼一样大，跟天上的星星一样高。接着他跟我讲，将来他想干一门生意，一个小小的营生，说不定能长成一家大集团。他说他要做这一行的巨头。我没笑。那雪人堆得真不错。"},"innocent":{"tw":[["innocence",4],["free",0],["lamb",3],["guilty",1],["victim",6],["barren",0],["virgin",3],["murder",6]],"en":"The court found the young man innocent of the murder, and the whole room let out a long breath. He had spent two years in prison for a crime he did not do, and his innocence was finally clear. The real guilty man had never been caught, and the victim's family sat in silence. The judge set the young man free that morning. Outside, a lamb stood in a barren field, and he looked at it for a long time. Some land nearby was still virgin ground, never built on. He said he wanted to go somewhere quiet and start again.","zh":"法庭判定那年轻人没犯那桩凶案，整间屋子都长长松了口气。他为一件没做过的事在牢里待了两年，如今终于是清白的了。真正有罪的人一直没抓到，受害者的家属默默坐着。那天早上法官把那年轻人放了。外面，一只小羊站在荒地里，他看了它很久。附近还有一片未开垦的地，从没盖过房子。他说他想找个安静的地方，从头再来。"},"justice":{"tw":[["judicial",4],["judge",0],["right",3],["official",2],["law",6],["jurist",0],["magistrate",3],["rights",6]],"en":"The old magistrate had spent his whole life in the service of justice, and he knew every corner of the law. He was a jurist first and an official second. In his court the judge would listen to both sides and then state the right of each person. He said the judicial system was slow, but it was the only wall between people and force. He would not bend a rule for a friend. When the young clerk asked him what rights really meant, he thought for a moment and said they meant that no one was above the law. Then he went back to his papers.","zh":"那位老治安法官一辈子都在为公道做事，法律的每个角落他都熟。他先是法学家，其次才是官员。在他的法庭上，法官会先听完两边的话，再说清每个人应有的权利。他说这套司法体系是慢，可它是挡在百姓和强权之间的唯一一道墙。他绝不会为朋友通融一条规矩。年轻的书记员问他，权利到底是什么意思，他想了一会儿说，意思就是没有人能高过法律。然后他又低头看自己的材料去了。"},"damage":{"tw":[["hurt",0],["break",3],["change",2],["cause",6],["price",0],["burn",3],["cost",2],["impact",6],["wrong",0]],"en":"The hail did more damage to the garden than anything in years. It would break a young stem in a second, and the cold could burn a whole row of beans. My father said we should not change the plan because of one bad night. He counted the price of every lost plant and wrote it in his book. The real cost was not money, he said, but the time we had put in. I asked what had caused it, and he said the wrong wind at the wrong hour. The impact on the field next door was even worse. Nobody was hurt, and for that he was grateful.","zh":"这场冰雹对园子的损害比这些年任何一次都大。它一眨眼就能打折一根嫩枝，寒气还能把一整垄豆子烧死。我爸说不能因为一晚上不顺就改计划。他把每一棵损失掉的苗值多少钱都算了一遍，记在本子上。他说真正的代价不是钱，是我们搭进去的时间。我问是什么造成的，他说是错的风赶上了错的时辰。隔壁那块田受的影响更大。没人受伤，为此他心怀感激。"},"deck":{"tw":[["floor",0],["ornament",3],["beat",2],["roof",6],["decorate",2],["plume",3],["pack",2],["rear",6],["dump",0]],"en":"The old ferry had a wooden deck that smelled of salt and rope. We would pack our bags at the rear and sit there for the whole crossing. My mother liked to decorate the rail with a small ornament she carried, a little brass bird with a plume. Below us the engine would beat like a slow heart, and the floor shook under our feet. From the roof of the cabin you could see the whole bay. Once a man tried to dump a bag of rubbish over the side, and the captain stopped him. We reached the far shore just before dark.","zh":"那艘老渡轮的甲板是木头的，闻着有盐和绳子的味道。我们把包堆在后头，整趟航程就坐在那儿。我妈喜欢用她随身带的一个小饰物装点栏杆，那是只带羽冠的小铜鸟。下面发动机一起一伏，像颗慢下来的心，脚下的甲板直颤。从舱顶上能看见整个海湾。有一回一个人想把一袋垃圾倒进海里，被船长拦住了。天快黑时我们到了对岸。"},"depress":{"tw":[["lower",2],["chill",3],["change",2],["elate",1],["stagnate",6],["dismay",0],["discourage",2],["deflate",6],["demoralise",0]],"en":"The long grey winter began to depress the whole town. Every week seemed to lower the mood a little more, and the cold would chill any plan we made. Work would stagnate, and the shops grew quiet. The failure of the mill did not elate anyone, though some had hoped for change. My father tried not to discourage us, but I saw his dismay in the way he read the paper. He said a bad season could deflate a man faster than any debt. Then one morning the sun came out, and it seemed to demoralise nobody. Everyone walked a little faster.","zh":"漫长灰暗的冬天开始让整座镇子都蔫下来。每过一周，心情就好像又低落一分，寒气也把我们的任何打算都冻住。活儿停滞，铺子也冷清。磨坊倒闭没让谁高兴起来，虽然有些人本来盼着有变化。我爸尽力不让我们泄气，可从他看报的样子里我看得出他的沮丧。他说一个坏年景比任何债务都更快让人垮掉。后来有天早上太阳出来了，好像谁都没有被打击到。大家的脚步都轻快了一点。"},"design":{"tw":[["figure",0],["cut",3],["goal",2],["model",6],["plan",2],["mind",3],["intend",2],["architecture",6],["intent",0]],"en":"The design of the little chair began on the back of an envelope. My uncle would figure out each angle in his mind before he cut a single piece of wood. His plan was simple, and his only goal was that a child could carry it. He made a small model first, out of paper, and then changed the shape twice. He had once studied architecture, and it showed in the way he talked about light. I do not think he ever intended to sell it; it was for his own granddaughter. When it was finished, the intent behind every line was clear.","zh":"那把小板凳的设计是从一个信封背面开始的。我叔在下第一刀之前，会先在脑子里把每个角度算清楚。他的方案很简单，唯一的要求就是小孩子能拎得动。他先用纸做了个小模型，又把形状改了两回。他从前学过建筑，一谈光线就看得出。我想他从没打算把它卖掉，那是给他自己孙女的。做成之后，每一条线背后要表达什么都很清楚。"},"detail":{"tw":[["particular",0],["respect",3],["assign",2],["description",6],["item",0],["highlight",3],["elaborate",2],["illustrate",6],["contingent",0]],"en":"The teacher asked us to describe every detail of the old bridge, and to illustrate it with a drawing. She would assign one part to each student, so nobody had too much to do. My item was the stone arch, and I had to write a full description of how it was built. One particular problem was the height, which was contingent on the river below. I tried to highlight the clever way the blocks fitted together. An older student could elaborate on the history, and I listened carefully. Without respect for the small things, she said, a bridge would fall.","zh":"老师让我们把那座老桥的每个细节都描述出来，还要画图说明。她把各部分分给每个学生，谁也不用做太多。我分到的是石拱，得写一篇完整的说明，讲它是怎么砌起来的。特别是高度这一项有讲究，得看下面那条河。我尽量突出那些石块拼合得有多巧。一个高年级的同学还能把来历讲得更细，我认真听着。她说，不把那些小地方当回事，桥就会塌。"},"develop":{"tw":[["break",0],["age",3],["better",2],["improve",6],["grow",3],["build",3],["change",2],["focus",6],["prepare",0]],"en":"My aunt began to develop her small garden the year she turned sixty. She would prepare the soil in March and then let everything grow on its own. The plan was to improve the worst corner first, where the old wall had begun to break. As the plants age, she said, the garden will change in ways you cannot control. She liked to build a new bed each spring and give away what she could not use. Her focus was always on the soil, never on the flowers. I watched that garden get better year after year, and I began to understand patience.","zh":"我姑姑六十岁那年，开始打理她那一小片园子。她三月里整好土，然后就任东西自己长。打算先把最差的那个角落改好，那里的老墙已经开始塌了。她说，苗一上年纪，园子就会往你控制不了的方向变。她喜欢每年春天新砌一垄苗床，用不完的送人。她始终盯着的是土，从来不是花。我眼看着那片园子一年比一年好，也就慢慢懂了什么叫耐心。"},"discipline":{"tw":[["check",0],["major",3],["develop",2],["exercise",6],["field",0],["mortify",3],["punish",2],["skill",6],["study",0]],"en":"The old music teacher had a discipline that none of us liked at the time. She would check our hands before every lesson and make us do the same exercise fifty times. If we played a wrong note, she would not punish us, but she would make us play it again until it was right. Her major point was that skill comes from habit, not from talent. She said it would develop only with years of quiet work. Once she had to mortify a boy in front of the class. She had given her whole life to this one field of study. I still hear her voice when I sit down to play.","zh":"那位老音乐老师的规矩，我们当时谁都不喜欢。每节课前她都要看我们的手，让我们把同一个练习做五十遍。弹错一个音她不会罚我们，但要我们一直弹到对为止。她的要点是：本事来自习惯，不是天赋。她说这东西只有靠一年年安静的苦练才长得出来。有一回她不得不当着全班的面让一个男孩下不来台。她把一辈子都给了这一门学问。如今我一坐下弹琴，还能听见她的声音。"},"dust":{"tw":[["scatter",0],["spray",3],["clean",2],["smoke",6],["disperse",0],["slack",3],["cover",2],["cloud",6],["dot",0]],"en":"A thin layer of dust lay over everything in the attic, and the light showed every dot of it. My mother would spray the shelves with water before she began, so the dust would not scatter into the air. Then she would clean each box and cover it again with cloth. Out of the small window a cloud of smoke rose from a garden fire and began to disperse over the roofs. She said you should never let the work go slack, or it would take twice as long. By evening the room smelled of soap and old paper. I carried the boxes down and put them in the sun.","zh":"阁楼里所有东西上都蒙着一层薄薄的灰，光一照，每一个小点都看得见。我妈动手前会先给架子喷点水，免得灰尘四处乱飞。然后她把每个箱子擦干净，再用布盖好。从小窗望出去，园子里烧火的一团烟升起来，在屋顶上慢慢散开。她说这活儿绝不能松着干，不然得多花一倍工夫。到傍晚，屋里一股肥皂和旧纸的味道。我把箱子搬下去，搁在太阳底下。"},"ease":{"tw":[["comfort",2],["leisure",3],["help",2],["pressure",6],["rest",0],["reprieve",3],["travel",2],["demand",6],["relief",0]],"en":"After the busy season my father would travel north for a week, and the ease of those days stayed with him all year. There was no pressure to answer the telephone, no demand from anyone. He would rest in a chair by the water and take his comfort from the small things: tea, bread, the sound of birds. For once he had nothing but leisure. It was a short reprieve, and he knew it. My mother said the real help was not the holiday but the memory of it. For a few days he seemed to have no duties at all. He came home slower and kinder, and the relief lasted until the first Monday.","zh":"忙季一过，我爸就会往北走一个星期，那几天的安逸能陪他一整年。没有必须接电话的压力，也没人向他提要求。他会坐在水边的椅子上歇着，从茶、面包、鸟叫这些小东西里找舒服。这不过是短暂的喘息，他心里清楚。我妈说真正管用的不是那趟休假，而是关于它的记忆。有那么几天，他像是全无负担。他回家时慢了些，也温和了些，这份轻松一直撑到第一个周一。"},"embarrass":{"tw":[["block",0],["check",3],["prevent",2],["humiliate",6],["obstruct",0],["hang",3],["upset",2],["distract",6],["blockade",0]],"en":"I did not mean to embarrass my sister at the table, but my joke went too far. Her face went red, and it had upset her more than I expected. A silence seemed to block the whole room. It felt like a blockade around the table. My mother tried to distract us with a story, but that only made it worse. I wanted to hang my head and leave. My father told me later that a careless word can humiliate someone long after the meal. He said we should check ourselves first, not try to prevent every joke. To obstruct the silence, he finally said something kind, and slowly the talking came back to the table.","zh":"我并不是有意在饭桌上让我妹妹难堪，可我的玩笑开过了头。她脸红了，这事让她难受的程度超出我的预料。屋里像是被一阵沉默堵住了，那桌子四周仿佛被封锁了一样。我妈想讲个故事把大家的心思岔开，结果只更糟。我恨不得低下头走开。事后我爸跟我说，一句不小心的话能在饭后很久还让人抬不起头。他说，先得管住自己，而不是去堵每一个玩笑。为了打破那片沉默，他终于说了句温和的话，桌上的话头才慢慢回来了。"},"entertain":{"tw":[["hold",0],["amuse",3],["feel",2],["impress",6],["nurse",0],["host",3],["contemplate",2],["invite",6],["harbor",0]],"en":"My grandmother loved to entertain, and she would invite half the street to eat with us. She could hold a room for hours with her stories, and she never tired of trying to amuse the children. She would nurse a cup of tea all evening and watch everyone from her chair. It was hard to impress her, but she was easily pleased. I would feel warm just watching her. As host she had one rule: nobody left hungry, and nobody left early. I think she would harbor a small sadness when the last guest went home. She would sit and contemplate the empty plates, then start clearing them.","zh":"我奶奶最爱招待客人，半条街的人她都请来跟我们一起吃饭。她靠讲故事能把一屋子人拢住好几个钟头，逗孩子玩也从不觉累。她会捧着一杯茶喝一整晚，坐在椅子上看着大家。要讨她一句夸很难，可她特别容易满足。光看着她，我心里就暖暖的。作为主人她只有一条规矩：谁都不许饿着走，谁都不许早走。我猜最后一个客人回家时，她心里会藏着一丝失落。她会坐着看那些空盘子，然后动手收拾。"},"escape":{"tw":[["miss",0],["break",3],["issue",2],["attempt",6],["run",0],["shake",3],["leave",2],["kill",6],["flight",0]],"en":"The bird had come in through the open window and could not find its way out. It would run along the glass and beat its wings, trying to escape. Every attempt failed, and I was afraid it would break a wing or kill itself on the wall. My father told me to leave the room quiet and not to shake the curtain. He said the real issue was that the bird could not see the opening. Then it found the gap and was gone in a single flight. I sat down, my hands still shaking, and missed it at once. The room felt larger and emptier than before.","zh":"那只鸟从开着的窗户飞了进来，找不到出去的路。它沿着玻璃一路扑腾，想逃出去。每一次尝试都失败了，我怕它会在墙上撞断翅膀。我爸让我把屋子放安静，别去晃窗帘。他说真正的问题是它看不见那个出口。后来它找到了缝隙，一飞就不见了。我坐下来，手还在抖，立刻就有点想它。屋子显得比以前更大、更空了。"},"establish":{"tw":[["base",0],["fix",3],["open",2],["abolish",1],["ensure",6],["build",3],["confirm",2],["aim",6],["ground",0]],"en":"A group of parents wanted to establish a small school in the empty hall. First they had to build a base of support, and then fix a date for the first meeting. They would open the doors on a Saturday and ensure that every child could come free. The aim was simple: teach the youngest ones to read before they turned seven. Someone asked whether they should abolish the old rule about uniforms, and everyone laughed. They had to confirm the teacher's pay and find a place on the ground for a small garden. A year later the school was full.","zh":"一群家长想在空出来的礼堂里办一所小学校。他们得先攒起一批支持的人，再定下头一次开会的日子。他们打算周六开门，并且保证每个孩子都能免费来。目标很简单：让最小的那些孩子在七岁前学会认字。有人问要不要把关于校服的老规矩废掉，大家都笑了。他们还得敲定老师的报酬，并在空地上找块地方弄个小园子。一年之后，学校招满了。"},"exchange":{"tw":[["change",2],["break",3],["conversation",2],["stock",6],["replace",2],["sell",3],["commerce",2],["closed",6],["switch",0]],"en":"At the market I wanted to exchange a shirt for a larger one, but the stall was closed. The woman said she could replace it, though she had no other colour in stock. We had a short conversation about the size and the price, and she was kind. She would not sell me the wrong one twice, she said, and she refused to take a break until it was sorted. In the end she offered a switch: a shirt for a coat, and I paid the difference. It was honest commerce, old style. When I left, she said the change was nothing and waved me away.","zh":"在市场上我想把一件衬衫换成大一号的，可那摊子关着门。那位女士说可以给我换，只是店里没有别的颜色了。我们为尺码和价钱短聊了几句，她人很好。她说绝不会把错的东西卖我两回，事没办完她也不肯歇。最后她提了个换法：衬衫换外套，差价我补。这是老派的实在买卖。我走的时候，她说这点零头不算什么，挥手让我走了。"},"exhaust":{"tw":[["beat",0],["blow",3],["empty",2],["brake",6],["tire",0],["kill",3],["gas",2],["fuel",6],["release",0]],"en":"The old van's exhaust was loud, and every time he pressed the brake you could hear it. My father said the gas was going straight out of the pipe, wasting fuel with every mile. He would beat the pipe with a hammer to test it, and a black blow of smoke would come out. The tank was almost empty, so we had to stop for more. The long drive home began to tire him, and I could see it in his face. He would release the pedal and let the van roll down the hill. It was slower than walking, but it never killed us.","zh":"那辆旧货车的排气管很响，他每次踩刹车你都听得见。我爸说燃气直接从管子里跑掉了，每开一英里都在浪费油。他会用锤子敲敲管子试试，一股黑烟就冒出来。油箱快见底了，我们只好停下来加油。长途往回开，他开始累了，从他脸上看得出来。他会松开踏板，让车顺着坡溜下去。比走路还慢，可它到底没把我们怎么样。"},"familiar":{"tw":[["fellow",0],["date",3],["friend",2],["strange",1],["look",6],["associate",0],["spirit",2],["often",6],["companion",0]],"en":"His face looked familiar, though I could not put a date on it. He was a fellow I had known at school, a friend of my older brother. We would often meet at the corner shop, back when that strange little clock hung over the door. He had the same look about him, the same quiet spirit. I did not want to ask his name, and he did not give it. Later I told my companion that I could not associate the face with any event. She laughed and said it was just someone I had seen in a dream.","zh":"他的脸看着眼熟，可我想不起是什么时候的事。他是我上学时认识的一个同学，我哥的朋友。从前门上方还挂着那只怪模怪样的小钟时，我们常在街角那家店碰见。他神情没变，还是那副安静的样子。我不想问他的名字，他也没说。后来我跟同伴说，这张脸我配不上任何一件具体的事。她笑了，说那不过是我在梦里见过的人罢了。"},"fancy":{"tw":[["figure",0],["bubble",3],["imagine",2],["plain",1],["fun",6],["picture",0],["desire",2],["dress",6],["see",0]],"en":"My little cousin has a fancy that will not leave her: she wants to be a dancer. She will figure out the steps in her head and then perform them for anyone who will watch. When she talks about it, her words bubble over and she cannot stop. Her parents, who are plain people, do not quite see the point. But they never laugh, and they let her imagine whatever she likes. It is fun to watch her picture herself on a huge stage. I think her real desire is not the dance but the light. She would dress for it in a paper crown.","zh":"我的小表妹心里有个赶不走的念头：她想当舞者。她会在脑子里把步子想好，然后表演给任何愿意看的人。一谈起这个，她的话就往外冒，收都收不住。她父母都是本分人，不太明白这有什么意义。可他们从不笑话她，任她怎么想就怎么想。看她把自己想成站在大舞台上，挺有意思。我觉得她真正想要的不是跳舞，而是那束光。她会戴一顶纸做的皇冠当作行头。"},"fault":{"tw":[["break",0],["hole",3],["charge",2],["lie",6],["mistake",0],["slip",3],["serve",2],["problem",6],["blame",0]],"en":"The fault was not in the machine but in the way we used it. My father would charge the battery all night, which was his first mistake. There was a small hole in the cable, and the current would slip out and leave it dead by morning. He would lie awake worrying about the problem instead of checking the wire. On the court that evening I served a double fault, and my partner tried to blame the wind. Then he slipped and fell, and we both laughed. The cable did not break, but it might have. A second serve is like a second chance.","zh":"毛病不在机器上，而在我们用的方式上。我爸会把电池充一整夜，这就是他的头一个错。电缆上有个小洞，电会悄悄漏掉，到早上就一点不剩。他会躺着为这事发愁，却不去查那根线。那天傍晚在球场上我发球双误，搭档想把责任推给风。接着他脚下一滑摔了，我们俩都笑了。那根电缆没断，差一点就断了。第二发球就像第二次机会。"},"feature":{"tw":[["sport",3],["bear",3],["article",2],["screen",6],["characteristic",0],["carry",3],["property",2],["original",6],["boast",0]],"en":"The park's best feature was the long line of trees that carried shade over the path all summer. A local paper had written an article about it, and the writer seemed to boast that nothing like it existed. The original plan, from a hundred years ago, had been to leave the ground open for sport. Nowadays children come to play football where the old screen of trees once stood. I could not bear the noise on a Sunday, but I understood the property's value. Every small characteristic of the place had been paid for by the town. It is the only green space we have.","zh":"这座公园最出色的地方，是那排长长的树，整个夏天把阴凉铺在小路上。本地一家报纸为它写过一篇文章，作者还夸口说别处再没有这样的地方。一百年前最初的设计，是想把这块地空出来做运动场。如今孩子们就在从前那片树墙的地方踢球。周日那么吵我实在受不了，可我明白这块地的价值。这地方每一处小小的特点，都是镇上花钱换来的。这是我们仅剩的一片绿地。"},"fence":{"tw":[["wall",3],["hedge",3],["protect",2],["gate",6],["argue",0],["oppose",3],["receive",2],["inside",6],["surround",0]],"en":"Our neighbours wanted to build a low fence along the wall at the back of the garden. My father would argue that a hedge was better, because it would protect the birds. They did not oppose the idea, but they wanted a gate so the postman could come inside. In the end we agreed to surround the whole plot with both: a fence in front and hedge behind. I helped to receive the wood when the lorry came. It took two weekends, and my hands were sore for a week. Now the birds sit on the fence and the cats cannot get in.","zh":"邻居想沿着园子后头那堵墙修一道矮栅栏。我爸会说种一排树篱更好，因为那能护住鸟。他们不反对这个主意，但想要一扇门，好让邮差能进院子。最后我们商量好两种一起上，把整块地围起来：前面栅栏，后面树篱。货车来时我帮着收货。干了两个周末，我的手疼了一个星期。现在鸟落在栅栏上，猫也进不来了。"},"file":{"tw":[["charge",0],["column",3],["line",2],["copy",6],["register",0],["rasp",3],["record",2],["client",6],["lodge",0]],"en":"The doctor kept a thick file on every client, and each one had its own record. She would write a line at the top, then a column of dates down the side. When a new patient came, she would charge the office for a copy of the notes. The old metal cabinet had a drawer that would rasp when she opened it. She told me to lodge the form with the front desk before I left. With a hard file she could smooth the rough edge of the new card. Every name had to go into the register as well. She was careful, and she never lost a single page.","zh":"医生给每个病人留一份厚厚的档案，每人都有自己的记录。她会在最上面写一行，再沿边写下一列日期。来了新病人，她会向诊所收一份副本的费用。那个旧铁柜的抽屉一拉开就发出刺耳的响声。她让我走之前把表格交到前台去登记。用一把硬锉刀，她能把新卡片的毛边磨平。每个名字也都要写进登记簿。她做事仔细，一页都没丢过。"},"flag":{"tw":[["pin",0],["bag",3],["list",2],["emblem",6],["sag",0],["standard",3],["mark",2],["red",6],["droop",0]],"en":"A flag hung over the village hall, and by afternoon the wet cloth began to droop. It had been made by hand, with a small emblem in the corner that nobody could name. My mother would pin a paper list under it, showing who had paid for the food. The standard of the cloth was poor, and the red colour had begun to sag and run. Someone had left a bag of shopping in the corner, with a mark on the side in black ink. We took the flag down before the rain came. It is in a box in the loft now, waiting for next year.","zh":"村礼堂上方挂着一面旗，到了下午，湿透的布开始往下垂。那是手工做的，角落有个谁也说不清是什么的小标记。我妈会在旗子下面钉一张纸单，写明谁付了伙食钱。这块布的成色不好，红色已经开始松垮、晕开。有人把一个购物袋落在角落里，侧面用黑墨水做了个记号。我们在下雨前把旗子取了下来。它现在收在阁楼的箱子里，等着明年。"},"flip":{"tw":[["pass",0],["lag",3],["change",2],["tack",6],["sky",0],["submarine",3],["move",2],["poke",6],["throw",2]],"en":"My brother would flip stones across the water and count how many times they hit. He had a small toy submarine that he would throw in and then poke with a stick. The sky was grey, and the wind would change every few minutes. I liked to watch the light move on the surface while the afternoon began to lag. He wanted to tack a paper flag to the submarine with tape, and it would not stay on. A boat passed in the distance, and he waved. The day went by so slowly that I did not notice the cold. We stayed until our mother called us home.","zh":"我弟会往水面上打水漂，一下一下数着石头点了多少次水。他有只小玩具潜艇，扔进水里，再用棍子去捅。天是灰的，风每过几分钟就换个向。我喜欢看光在水面上移动，看着下午一点点拖长。他想用胶带在潜艇上贴面小纸旗，怎么都粘不住。远处有条船经过，他挥了挥手。那一天过得太慢，我都没觉出冷来。我们一直待到妈妈喊我们回家。"},"flow":{"tw":[["course",2],["waste",3],["move",2],["stream",6],["fall",0],["flood",3],["rate",2],["upstream",6],["feed",0]],"en":"The stream behind our house would flow fast after heavy rain and then slow to almost nothing. Its course changed a little every year, cutting into the bank on one side. My father said the water was never wasted, even when it seemed to fall away in summer. He built a small gate to feed the garden and to keep the rate steady. Once a flood came in the night and moved every stone downstream. I used to walk upstream and watch the current. It taught me that nothing stays still. In spring you could hear it from the bedroom window.","zh":"屋后那条小溪下过大雨就流得急，过后又慢得几乎不动。它每年都会稍微改道，把一边的岸啃掉一点。我爸说这水从没白流，哪怕夏天看着像是要没了。他修了一道小闸门，用来浇园子，也让水流保持平稳。有一回夜里发了水，把每块石头都往下游冲了。我从前常往上游走，看着水流。它教给我一件事：什么都不会停着不动。春天的时候，在卧室窗边就能听见它。"},"frame":{"tw":[["build",0],["chase",3],["body",2],["structure",6],["figure",0],["vocabulary",3],["photograph",2],["window",6],["form",0]],"en":"The frame around the old photograph had come apart, and my grandfather wanted to build a new one himself. He would chase down every small piece of wood in the market until he found the right colour. The body of the frame was made of oak, and the structure was simple. From the window he could see the street while he worked. His figure bent over the table for hours, and his vocabulary of tools was small but sure. Slowly the shape began to form under his hands. He said a picture is only as good as what holds it.","zh":"那张老照片的相框散架了，爷爷想自己做一个新的。他会跑遍市场找每一小段木料，直到挑到合适的颜色。框身是橡木的，结构很简单。干活的时候，从窗户能看见街上。他弓着身子在桌边一坐就是几个钟头，他那套工具的词汇不多，却样样在行。形状慢慢在他手下成形。他说，一幅画的好坏，全看托着它的东西。"},"fry":{"tw":[["child",0],["orphan",3],["cook",2],["lamb",6],["kid",0],["peanut",3],["heat",2],["ginger",6],["minor",0]],"en":"On Sundays my mother would fry small pieces of lamb with ginger and a little oil. The heat had to be just right, or the meat would go hard. My little brother was still a child then, and he would stand on a chair to watch, asking questions the whole time. My father said he was a minor cook with a major appetite, and we all laughed. There was a kid from the next street, an orphan, who often ate with us. She liked the peanut sweets best. I learned to cook beside my mother, and I still use her pan.","zh":"每到星期天，我妈会用姜和一点油煎几块羊肉。火候得刚刚好，不然肉就发硬。那时我弟弟还是个孩子，他会踩在椅子上看，一路上问个不停。我爸说他是个小厨子，胃口倒不小，逗得我们全笑。隔壁街上有个孩子，是个孤儿，常来我们家吃饭。她最爱吃花生糖。我跟着我妈学会了做饭，到现在还用她那口锅。"},"goal":{"tw":[["end",2],["basket",3],["score",2],["forward",6],["finish",0],["purpose",3],["content",2],["minute",6],["destination",3]],"en":"The team had one goal: to finish the season without losing at home. In the last minute of the game the score was level, and the crowd stood up. The forward took the ball, moved past two players, and threw it toward the basket. It went in, and the noise was like nothing I had heard. Their purpose had been clear from the first day, and their coach was content with the way they played. The end of the match felt less like a destination than a door opening. I walked home slowly, still hearing the cheering. For once, nobody talked about next year.","zh":"这支队伍只有一个目标：这个赛季在主场一场不输。比赛最后一分钟比分还是平的，观众都站了起来。前锋拿球，连过两人，把球投向篮筐。球进了，那阵声浪我从没听过。他们的目的从第一天起就很清楚，教练对他们的打法也满意。比赛结束不像到达了一个终点，倒像一扇门打开了。我慢慢走回家，耳边还是那片欢呼。这一回没人提明年的事。"},"grab":{"tw":[["catch",0],["fish",3],["move",2],["throw",6],["snap",0],["hook",3],["touch",2],["pull",6],["seize",0]],"en":"I had to grab the line before it went over the side of the boat. My grandfather would catch a fish with one hand and pull the hook out with the other. He told me never to throw the small ones back too hard, and never to touch the sharp end. The rod would snap if you moved too suddenly, he said, so you must wait. Then he would seize the moment and pull, and the fish would come up shining. We kept two for supper and let the rest go. On the way home I held the bag and said nothing.","zh":"我得在鱼线翻过船舷之前一把抓住它。我爷爷会一只手接住鱼，另一只手把鱼钩取下来。他叫我千万别把小鱼用力扔回去，也别去碰那个尖头。他说你要是猛地一动，鱼竿就会折，所以得等。然后他会抓住时机一拉，鱼就亮闪闪地出了水。我们留两条晚饭吃，其余的都放回去。回家路上我拎着袋子，一句话也没说。"},"guard":{"tw":[["hold",0],["patrol",3],["act",2],["army",6],["defend",0],["shepherd",3],["position",2],["base",6],["ward",0]],"en":"The guard walked his patrol every two hours, from the gate to the far wall. His job was to hold the position and to act if anything moved in the dark. He had once been in the army, and he said a quiet night was the best kind. His only company was a dog that would defend the yard from strangers. Above him, on the roof, a stone shepherd watched the empty fields. At the base of the stairs there was a small ward where the old men slept. He checked the doors twice and wrote it down. He never once had to use his keys.","zh":"那名守卫每两个钟头巡一趟，从大门口走到尽头的墙。他的差事就是守住岗位，夜里一有动静就得行动。他当年当过兵，说安静的夜是最好的夜。他唯一的伴儿是一条狗，会替他看住院子，不让生人靠近。在他头顶的屋脊上，一座石头的牧羊人望着空荡荡的田。楼梯底下有个小病房，几个老人睡在那儿。他把门查了两遍，记在本子上。他从没真用上过那串钥匙。"},"guide":{"tw":[["draw",0],["corner",3],["control",2],["search",6],["head",0],["hand",3],["direct",2],["web",6],["lead",0]],"en":"Our guide led us up a path that no map showed, and he would draw it in the air with his hand. At each corner he stopped and pointed, and we had to search for the marks he had left the year before. He liked to control the pace, so that nobody fell behind. He would direct the older walkers to the front and keep the young ones near him. Above us the web of paths spread over the hill. He said the head must decide, but the feet must lead. We reached the top before the clouds came. I have never trusted a map since.","zh":"我们的向导带我们走上一条地图上根本没有的路，他会用手在空中比划。每到一个拐角他就停下来指一指，我们得去找他去年留下的记号。他喜欢把节奏攥在手里，免得有人掉队。他会让年纪大的走前面，把年轻人留在自己身边。我们头上，一张小路织成的网铺满山坡。他说脑子负责决定，脚负责带路。我们在云上来之前到了山顶。从那以后我就再没信过地图。"},"harm":{"tw":[["hurt",0],["burn",3],["change",2],["cause",6],["damage",0],["run",3],["injure",2],["risk",6],["trauma",0]],"en":"The bleach was old, and nobody had thought it could do any harm. My sister mixed it with another cleaner, and the smell began to burn our eyes. We had to run out into the yard, and for a while we could not breathe. My sister's throat hurt for days. The doctor said there was no lasting damage, but the fear stayed with us. A careless mistake can injure more than the body; it can leave a kind of trauma. The cause was only two bottles standing together. My mother said we should change the way we kept the bottles, and she was right. We never took that risk again. I still open a window before I clean.","zh":"那瓶漂白水放得太久了，谁也没想到它还会伤人。我妹妹把它跟另一种清洁剂兑在一起，那股味开始熏眼睛。我们只好跑进院子，好一会儿都喘不上气。我妹妹的嗓子疼了好几天。医生说没有留下什么后患，可那份害怕一直跟着我们。一个疏忽造成的错，伤的往往不只是身体，还能留下一种创伤。我妈说收纳这些瓶子的方式得改，她说得对。我们再也不冒这个险了。到现在我打扫前都先开窗。"},"heap":{"tw":[["bus",0],["flood",3],["arrange",2],["pile",6],["deal",0],["shock",3],["fill",2],["slag",6],["lot",0]],"en":"There was a heap of old chairs in the corner of the warehouse, and nobody would arrange them. A flood of boxes had come in the same week, and the whole floor was a mess. The manager said we had a lot to deal with, and this heap was only the start. Each pile had to be counted and marked before it went out. The bus came at six to take the first load, and we had to fill it before then. One box fell and gave us a shock. Under the wood there was a bag of slag from the old works, heavy as stone.","zh":"仓库角落里堆着一堆旧椅子，谁都不愿去归置。同一周又来了一大批箱子，整个地面乱成一团。经理说我们有一大堆事要处理，这堆椅子还只是个开头。每一摞都得点数、做标记，才能发出去。班车六点来拉头一批，我们得在那之前装满。一个箱子掉下来，把我们吓一跳。木头底下还有一袋旧厂子留下的矿渣，沉得像石头。"},"image":{"tw":[["double",0],["guy",3],["imagine",2],["display",6],["figure",0],["concentrate",3],["model",2],["vision",6],["picture",0]],"en":"The image on the screen was not the one I had taken. In the display there were two figures instead of one, a double of the old man at the door. I tried to imagine how it had happened, but I could not concentrate. The guy in the next room said it was a fault in the camera, not in the light. His own model of the scene was simple: a mirror, a window, and a long wait. I wanted a clear picture, and now I had a vision of something that was never there. I turned the screen off and went out for a walk.","zh":"屏幕上那张影像不是我拍的。画面里不是一个人，而是两个身影，门边那个老汉被照成了双份。我想弄明白是怎么回事，可怎么也集中不了精神。隔壁那位说，是相机出了毛病，不是光的问题。他对这场景的解释很简单：一面镜子、一扇窗，还有漫长的等待。我本想拍一张清清楚楚的照片，结果眼前却出现了根本不存在的东西。我关掉屏幕，出门走了走。"},"influence":{"tw":[["shape",0],["carry",3],["cause",2],["particular",6],["work",0],["fix",3],["power",2],["regard",6],["charm",0]],"en":"The old teacher had an influence that reached far beyond her classroom. She would shape the way we thought about work, and she carried her calm into every room. I do not think she ever tried to cause anyone to change; she simply set an example. In those days a particular kind of respect was given to people who fixed things with their hands. Her power came from patience, not from fear. I had never met anyone with so little charm and so much quiet weight. Years later I still regard her as the best teacher I had. She changed how I read a book.","zh":"那位老教师的影响远远超出了她那间教室。她会影响我们对干活这件事的看法，还把她的镇定带到每一间屋子里。我想她从没想过要去促使谁改变，只是自己做了个榜样。那时候，人们对那些靠双手修东西的人有一种特别的敬重。她的力量来自耐心，不是来自让人害怕。我从没见过谁身上这么少花哨的吸引力，却又这么有分量。多年以后我仍把她看作我遇到过最好的老师。是她改变了我读书的方式。"},"interrupt":{"tw":[["break",0],["cut",3],["act",2],["synchronize",6],["disturb",0],["freeze",3],["end",2],["interfere",6],["disrupt",0]],"en":"Please do not interrupt me while I am reading, my teacher would say. If someone did break the silence, she would cut the lesson short and start again. It was not an act of anger; she simply wanted us to listen. She would synchronize the end of the lesson with the bell, so that nothing was ever rushed. I learned never to disturb a person who is thinking. When the bell came in the middle of a sentence, she would freeze, then finish without a word. She said a good listener must not interfere with the speaker's train of thought. Now, when the telephone disrupts my work, I hear her voice and stop.","zh":"我读书的时候请别打断我，我的老师总会这么说。要是谁真把那份安静打破了，她就把课砍短，从头再来。这不是发脾气，她只是要我们学会听。她会把下课和铃声同步好，从不慌慌张张。我学会了绝不打扰正在想事的人。铃在句子中间响起来时，她会顿住，然后一言不发把话说完。她说，好的听者不能去搅乱说话人的思路。如今电话打断我的工作时，我就听见她的声音，停下来。"},"invite":{"tw":[["receive",0],["see",3],["interact",2],["urge",6],["tempt",3],["assume",3],["request",2],["participate",6],["bid",0]],"en":"We decided to invite the whole street to the party, and my mother would receive every answer by hand. It was hard to see who would actually come. She would urge the shy ones to participate and tell them there was no need to bring anything. I was tempted to assume nobody would come at all, but I was wrong. A single request from my father, written on a card, brought almost everyone. It was strange to watch neighbours interact who had never spoken. I did not see one person who stayed away. There was a small bid for the last piece of cake, and we all laughed.","zh":"我们决定把整条街的人都请来聚会，回话都由我妈一手收着。谁真会来，实在说不准。她会劝那些腼腆的人也来参加，还说不用带任何东西。我差点就认定一个都不会来，结果我想错了。我爸写在一张卡片上的一句邀请，几乎把人都请来了。看着那些从没说过话的邻居互相打交道，挺奇怪的。我没见着一个人躲着不来。最后一块蛋糕还有过一番小小的争抢，我们都笑了。"},"jam":{"tw":[["fix",0],["screen",3],["push",2],["hop",6],["hole",0],["dam",3],["stuff",2],["drum",6],["mess",0]],"en":"We made jam every autumn, and the kitchen always ended in a mess. My mother would push the fruit through a fine screen to take out the stones. There was a small hole in the cloth, so she would fix it with a pin. Sugar came from a big drum in the corner, and the smell filled the house. A few flies would hop about the window, and she would dam them off with a wet towel. The stuff was too hot to taste at first. By evening we had twelve jars and sticky hands. I still have one jar from that year.","zh":"每年秋天我们都做果酱，厨房最后总是一片狼藉。我妈会用细筛子把果肉挤过去，把果核滤掉。布上有小洞，她就拿别针别住。糖从角落里一口大桶里舀，那味道填满了整间屋子。几只苍蝇在窗边蹦来蹦去，她就用湿毛巾把它们挡住。那东西一开始烫得没法尝。到傍晚我们有了十二罐果酱和一双黏手。那一年的果酱我还留着一罐。"},"jaw":{"tw":[["visit",0],["chop",3],["bone",2],["neck",6],["chat",0],["crunch",3],["knock",2],["limb",6],["chew",0]],"en":"My uncle broke his jaw during a family football game, and he had to visit the hospital that night. He could not chew for a month, so everything had to be chopped into small pieces. The doctor said the bone would heal, but the neck and one limb were also bruised. It hurt to chat, and he would only nod. I could hear the crunch of ice in his glass all evening, and it made me wince. Then he would knock on the table to ask for something. For weeks he ate soup and watched us from the corner of the room. He never complained once.","zh":"我叔在一场家庭足球赛上摔断了下巴，当晚就得去医院。他一个月不能嚼东西，什么都要剁成小块。医生说骨头会好，可脖子和一条腿也青了。想聊天就疼，他只能点头。整晚我都能听见他杯子里冰块碎裂的声音，听得我直皱眉。他要什么都敲桌子。好几个星期他就喝汤，坐在屋角看着我们吃。他一句怨言都没有。"},"joy":{"tw":[["delight",0],["cheer",3],["feel",2],["sorrow",1],["pride",6],["pleasure",0],["exult",3],["love",6],["rejoice",0]],"en":"The birth of my cousin's daughter brought a joy into our family that lasted all winter. My grandmother would feel it most and would rejoice quietly, holding the baby for hours. She said the pleasure was in the small things: a hand, a sigh, the smell of milk. There was a little sorrow too, because my grandfather was not there to see it. But the pride in the room was stronger, and everyone began to cheer when the baby smiled. Her parents seemed to exult over every new sound she made. It was pure delight, and no one wanted the evening to end. They had waited a long time for this love.","zh":"我表姐添了个女儿，给家里带来的那份欢喜整个冬天都没消。我奶奶感受最深，她会安安静静地高兴上好一阵，孩子一抱就是几个钟头。她说那份快乐都在小地方：一只小手、一声轻叹、奶香味。也有一点伤感，因为我爷爷没能看到。可屋里的骄傲更浓，孩子一笑，大家都欢呼起来。她爸妈对她发出的每一点动静都乐得不行。那是纯粹的喜悦，谁都不想散场。这份爱，他们等得太久了。"},"deliver":{"tw":[["deliverance",4],["present",0],["drop",3],["pass",2],["send",6],["serve",3],["carry",6]],"en":"The postman had to deliver a heavy box before the shop opened. He would carry it up three floors, then pass it to my mother with a smile. Inside there was a small present from my aunt, who lived far away. She had to send it by sea, and it took six weeks to arrive. The paper was wet, so he had to drop it gently on the table. He said he liked to serve the same street for years, and that it felt like a small deliverance when the last parcel was gone.","zh":"铺子开门前，邮递员得把一个沉箱子送来。他会把它搬上三楼，笑着递给我妈。里面是姑姑寄来的一件小礼物，她住得很远。东西只能走海路寄，用了六个星期。纸是湿的，他只好轻轻放到桌上。他说他喜欢在同一条街上干上好多年，送完最后一个包裹时，像卸下了一桩小小的负担。"},"evidence":{"tw":[["evident",4],["prove",0],["testify",2],["testimony",6],["demonstrate",0],["proof",6],["manifest",0]],"en":"The police found new evidence near the old bridge. It was evident from the marks on the rail that someone had climbed there that night. A boy came to testify, and his testimony was short and clear. He could demonstrate exactly where the man had stood, using his hands. The proof was not in one thing but in many small ones. The fear on his face was manifest, and nobody pushed him to say more. In the end, the case was closed on that quiet word. Nobody could prove more than that. I never learned what really happened.","zh":"警察在老桥附近找到了新证据。从栏杆上的痕迹看得出，那天夜里有人爬上去过。一个男孩来作证，他的证词简短清楚。他能用手比出那人当时站的位置。证据不在某一件事上，而在许多小事上。他脸上的害怕明明白白，谁也没逼他多说。最后案子就凭那句轻声的话结了。谁也证明不了更多。到底出了什么事，我始终没弄明白。"},"finance":{"tw":[["fiscal",4],["back",3],["pay",2],["minister",6],["fund",3],["credit",2],["cabinet",6]],"en":"The school had to sort out its finance before the new term. The man in charge of the fund sat in the back room with a thick book and tried to pay every bill on time. He said the fiscal year had been hard, and the cabinet that held the papers was almost empty. A bank offered a small credit, but it came with a heavy rate. The minister of the small church came to look at the roof, then left without a word. In the end, the parents raised the money themselves.","zh":"新学期开始前，学校得把财务理清楚。管基金的那个人坐在里屋，抱着一本厚账，尽量按时付清每一笔钱。他说这一财年不好过，装文件的柜子几乎空了。一家银行肯给一小笔贷款，可利息很重。小教堂的牧师来看过屋顶，一句话没说就走了。最后，是家长们自己凑的钱。"},"fruit":{"tw":[["fruition",4],["seed",3],["bear",2],["mango",6],["hip",3],["product",2],["corn",6]],"en":"The fruit from our old tree is small but sweet. My grandmother says it took ten years to come to fruition, and that a seed needs more than water to grow. The tree will bear only a few each year, and they taste a little like mango. The hip of the lower branch is thick and dark. Behind the house she grows corn in the field and sells it at the market as her best product. I think of that taste whenever I am far from home. It is a plain thing, but it stays.","zh":"老树结的果子不大，却很甜。奶奶说它等了十年才结果，还说一颗种子要长起来，光有水不够。这树每年只结几个，味道有点像芒果。下面那根枝的节又粗又黑。屋后地里她种玉米，拿到集市上卖，是她最好的出产。我离家在外时，总会想起那个味道。东西很普通，可就是忘不掉。"},"ignore":{"tw":[["ignorance",4],["cut",0],["slight",3],["reject",2],["know",1],["dismiss",0],["neglect",0]],"en":"I tried to ignore the small cut on my hand, but it would not stop stinging. My teacher told me not to neglect a thing just because it is slight, and not to dismiss a warning from someone who knows better. She said ignorance is not the same as a mistake, as long as you learn. I did not want to reject her advice, so I cleaned the wound and put on a cloth. The next day it was better. I never ignore a small cut now. Some lessons come from the smallest things.","zh":"我本想不去管手上那道小口子，可它一直火辣辣地疼。老师跟我说，别因为事情轻微就放着不管，也别把比你懂的人提的醒当耳旁风。她说，只要肯学，无知和犯错不是一回事。我不想把她的话顶回去，就洗干净伤口，敷了块布。第二天就好多了。现在我再不把一个小口子当没事。有些道理，是从最小的事里来的。"},"intend":{"tw":[["intent",4],["mean",3],["plan",3],["convince",6],["think",0],["calculate",3],["assure",6]],"en":"My brother and I intend to rebuild the old shed this summer. That is the plan, and it has been our intent since spring. I think we can finish it in ten days, though I cannot calculate the cost exactly. He tried to convince me that the roof would hold for another year, and I had to assure him that it would not. I did not mean to sound rude. We measured the boards twice and wrote every figure down, and when the rain came we were glad we had. The first afternoon went well, and by evening the new frame stood straight and solid.","zh":"我和哥哥打算今年夏天把那间旧棚子翻修一下。这就是我们的计划，从春天起我们就一直这么打算。我想十天能完工，虽然算不准要花多少钱。他劝我说屋顶还能撑一年，我只好跟他保证撑不住。我不是有意说得难听。我们把板子量了两遍，每个数都记了下来；下雨的时候，我们庆幸自己早做了准备。头一个下午干得挺顺，到傍晚新架子就立得又直又稳。"},"delight":{"tw":[["please",2],["endear",3],["satisfy",2],["cheer",6],["joy",0],["wallow",3],["laugh",6],["pleasure",2]],"en":"The baby took great delight in the paper hat, and would not let anyone take it away. Her laugh could please the whole room, and it was enough to endear her to every guest. My uncle tried to satisfy her with a spoon and a song, and when she finally grinned he began to cheer. The plain joy on her face made us all forget the rain outside. She would wallow in the cushions like a small animal. It was a simple pleasure, and it lasted the whole afternoon. Her mother said days like that were the best of the year.","zh":"那宝宝特别中意那顶纸帽子，谁也别想拿走。她一笑，满屋子人都高兴，一屋子的客人也就都喜欢上她了。我叔叔又想喂她一勺，又想唱歌哄她，等她终于咧嘴一笑，他就带头叫好。她脸上那种单纯的欢喜，让我们都忘了外头在下雨。她会像只小兽一样在靠垫里滚来滚去。这点小小的乐趣，撑了我们一整个下午。她妈妈说，这样的日子一年里最好。"},"desert":{"tw":[["abandon",0],["rat",3],["leave",2],["barren",6],["forsake",0],["ditch",3],["flee",2],["southern",6]],"en":"My uncle once told me about the year he worked in the far desert, where the land was barren and the wind never stopped. He had to leave a whole camp behind when the water ran out, and the men had to flee before dawn. It was hard to abandon so much gear, and one driver chose to forsake the truck and walk. They found an old ditch and slept in it, with rats running along the edge. That southern plain almost broke him. He said he would go again if he could. I have kept the small map he drew for me.","zh":"我叔叔跟我讲过他常年在远处沙漠里干活的那一年，那里的地光秃秃的，风从不停。水用完的时候，他只好丢下整个营地把人撤走，天亮前大家就都跑了。要扔下那么多装备真难，有个司机索性丢下卡车，一个人走。他们找到一条旧沟，就在里面睡下，老鼠沿着沟边窜。那片南边的荒原差点把他打垮。他说，要是还能去，他还会去。他给我画的那张小地图，我一直留着。"},"desire":{"tw":[["hope",3],["like",3],["request",2],["respect",6],["trust",0],["wish",3],["promise",6],["want",0]],"en":"My father had one desire for the house: he wanted a window that faced the sea. It was an old wish, and he liked to talk about it in the evening. When he put the request to the builder, the man did not laugh; he listened with real respect. I hope we can trust him to do the work well, my mother said, and my father promised to watch every step. We did not get the sea view, but the window is wide and bright. He says it is close enough. He sits by it most mornings, with his tea.","zh":"我爸对那房子只有一个心愿：他要一扇朝着海的窗。这是他很早就有的念想，傍晚的时候总爱念叨。他跟工匠提这个要求的时候，那人没笑，反而很认真听，带着真心的尊重。我妈说，希望能信得过他把活干好；我爸答应每一步都盯着。我们最后没得到海景，但那扇窗又宽又亮。他说，也差不多了。现在他大多数早上都端着茶坐在窗边。"},"direction":{"tw":[["charge",0],["address",3],["control",2],["toward",6],["focus",0],["rule",3],["position",2],["shift",6]],"en":"We walked in the wrong direction for nearly an hour before I stopped to ask an address. The man pointed toward the river and said we should keep the old tower on our left, but his rule was hard to follow. The map in my hand was out of date, and the position of the bridge had shifted since it was printed. I had to take charge of the way, since my sister had lost all focus. Her sense of control, I think, had gone with the sun. We found the street at last and laughed about it. Next time I will look it up before we leave.","zh":"我们朝着错的方向走了快一个钟头，我才停下来问地址。那人指着河那边，说把老塔留在左手边就行，可他这条规矩实在难照做。我手里那张地图已经过时，桥的位置打从印制出来以后就挪了。我只好自己把路揽下来，因为我妹妹已经完全没了方向感。我想，她的那点掌控感跟太阳一起落下去了。我们终于找到那条街，两个人还笑了半天。下次出门前，我一定先查好。"},"disgust":{"tw":[["revolt",0],["shock",3],["stimulate",2],["anger",6],["repel",2],["nausea",3],["dislike",2],["dismay",6]],"en":"The smell from the drain filled her with disgust, and she stepped back with a look of pure dismay. Nothing she had met that week could shock her more. A dead fish lay in the mud, and the sight seemed to repel even the dogs. Her anger was quiet but real: someone upstream had emptied a tank again. She felt a wave of nausea and had to look away. It was not mere dislike of dirt; she had watched this stream for years. The sight would revolt anyone who loved the place, and the smell was enough to stimulate the whole street into action. By Sunday the water ran clear again.","zh":"下水道里的气味让她一阵恶心，她倒退一步，脸上全是难受和失望。那一周她遇上的事，没有比这更叫她震惊的了。泥里躺着一条死鱼，那景象连狗都躲着走。她的火气不大，却是真的：又有人在上游倒了一罐脏东西。她一阵反胃，只好把脸转开。这不只是嫌脏，这条溪她看了好多年。那景象会让每个爱这个地方的人愤然，那股气味足以让整条街动起来。到星期天，水又清亮地流着了。"},"duck":{"tw":[["hedge",0],["quibble",3],["move",2],["crab",6],["skirt",0],["avoid",2],["lame",6],["dip",0]],"en":"A duck came out of the reeds and began to move along the bank, dipping its head at every step. It would skirt the low hedge and avoid the deep water where the current ran fast. My little brother wanted to quibble about whose turn it was to feed it, so I let him go first. A crab had crawled up on the stone, and he jumped back at the sight. The bird was lame in one leg, and it walked slowly, but it never stopped. We watched until it dipped into the pond and swam off. That was the best hour of the whole week.","zh":"一只鸭子从芦苇里钻出来，沿着岸边走，走一步点一下头。它绕开低矮的树篱，避开水流湍急的深水。我弟弟为轮到谁喂它争个没完，我让他先去。一只螃蟹爬上了石头，他一看就往后退。这鸟一条腿是瘸的，走得慢，可一步也没停。我们看着它一头扎进池塘，游走了。那是那一周里最好的一小时。"},"event":{"tw":[["issue",0],["act",3],["circumstance",2],["tournament",6],["effect",0],["product",3],["competition",6],["result",0]],"en":"The big event of our term was the town tournament, and every class had to enter. My teacher said the main issue was not winning but turning up ready. We had to act fast when one runner hurt his knee, and in those circumstances nobody argued about who took his place. The result was better than we had hoped, though the effect on the older students was the strangest part. Our little team had become a product of all that practice. The whole competition ended with a shared meal in the hall. I still have the small cup they gave us.","zh":"那个学期最要紧的活动就是镇上的锦标赛，每个班都得参加。老师说，关键不在赢，而在于到场时已经准备好。一个跑手伤了膝盖，我们只能马上应付；那种情况下，谁也没争该由谁顶上。结果比我们想的还好，不过最奇怪的是它对高年级学生的影响。我们这支小队，是那些练习一天天磨出来的东西。整场比赛最后以在礼堂里一起吃顿饭收场。他们发给我们的小奖杯，我还留着。"},"fashion":{"tw":[["manner",0],["cut",3],["vogue",2],["chic",6],["style",0],["fit",3],["glamour",6],["mode",0]],"en":"My sister worked in a shop where every coat had to be sold in a certain fashion. She could tell the vogue of a season from the cut of a sleeve, and she wore the plainest things in the most chic way. Her own style was simple: a good fit and a quiet colour, nothing more. Customers came for the glamour of the window and left with a better coat. Her manner with them never changed, whether they spent a lot or a little. That, she said, was the only mode worth keeping. I bought one jacket there and wore it for ten years.","zh":"我妹妹在一家店里做事，那里每件外套都得按一种讲究卖出去。她看一只袖子的裁剪，就知道这一季时兴什么；可她穿得最素，却最有味道。她自己的风格很简单：合身，颜色安静，别的都不需要。客人被橱窗里的光鲜吸引进来，走出去时手里是件更好的大衣。不管人家花多花少，她待人的态度都一样。她说，这是唯一值得留下的做法。我在那儿买过一件外套，穿了十年。"},"flood":{"tw":[["swamp",3],["debacle",3],["cover",2],["storm",6],["glut",0],["fill",2],["damage",6],["inundate",3]],"en":"After three days of rain the little river rose and began to flood the lower fields. The water seemed to swamp everything, and by morning it would cover the lane as well. My uncle called the whole thing a debacle: the market was already full, and a glut of wet grain would ruin the price. He and two men worked all night to fill bags with sand. The storm passed, but the damage was done, and the last field was inundated for a week. They saved the animals, at least. The barn still smells of wet wood, even in summer.","zh":"连下了三天雨，小河涨起来，开始淹下面的地。水仿佛把什么都吞了，到早上连小路也要盖住。我叔叔把这事叫做一场大溃败：本来就积压，再来一批湿谷子，价钱准得垮。他和两个人通宵装沙袋。暴风雨过去了，可损失已经造成，最下面那块地被泡了一个星期。至少牲口都保住了。那间谷仓到夏天还带着湿木头的味儿。"},"fool":{"tw":[["mark",0],["ass",3],["joke",2],["shoot",0],["play",2],["idiot",6],["mug",0]],"en":"At the village fair my cousin was an easy mark for every joke in the tent. He would play along with the oldest trick and then grin like an idiot, and the men would laugh and call him a name he did not mind. I bought him a mug of tea and told him to stop making such a fool of himself. In the next field a grey ass stood by the gate, and he went over to stroke it. Someone had a wooden gun and began to shoot at a row of cans. He won a small prize and was happy for the rest of the day.","zh":"在村里的集市上，我表弟成了帐篷里每个玩笑的现成对象。最老的把戏他也跟着玩，然后像傻子一样咧嘴笑，大人们哈哈一笑，给他起了个他并不在意的外号。我给他买了一杯茶，叫他别再这么出丑了。旁边那块地里有头灰驴站在门口，他跑过去摸它。有人拿一把木头枪，对着排成一溜的罐子打。他赢了个小奖品，高兴了一整天。"},"fox":{"tw":[["throw",0],["perplex",3],["spot",2],["channel",6],["confuse",0],["fur",2],["broadcast",6],["trick",0]],"en":"A red fox had made its home under the shed, and nobody could work out how it got in. My father would throw a stone near the gap and watch, but the animal was too quick to spot. The whole business began to perplex the neighbours, and the different stories only served to confuse them further. Someone said the local television channel would come and broadcast from the lane. My mother, who knew every trick, simply left a bowl of food by the hedge. That night the fox came out with its heavy winter fur and ate in the open.","zh":"一只红狐狸在棚子底下安了家，谁也想不出它是怎么钻进去的。我爸会往缝边上扔块石头看着，可那东西机灵得很，很难发现。这件事让邻居们越来越摸不着头脑，各说各的话，越传越糊涂。有人说本地的电视频道要来，在小路上做节目。我妈什么花招都懂，只是往树篱边放了一碗吃的。那天夜里，狐狸披着一身厚冬毛出来，就那么当众吃了起来。"},"fund":{"tw":[["store",0],["issue",3],["money",2],["raise",6],["stock",0],["budget",3],["support",2],["asset",6]],"en":"The school had a small fund for books, and every year the parents had to raise more money for it. The main issue was not the total but when the store of new stock would arrive. My mother kept the budget at home in a tin, and she would support any plan that did not touch the rent. She said a good name was the one asset you could not buy. We sold cakes in the hall for three weekends, and the shop gave us paper for free. By June the new shelves were full and the old tin was empty.","zh":"学校有一小笔买书的基金，家长们每年都得为它再筹些钱。要紧的不是总数，而是那批新书什么时候到。妈妈把预算放在家里一个铁盒里管着，凡是会动到房租的主意她都不赞成。她说，好名声是唯一买不到的家底。我们在礼堂里卖了三个周末的蛋糕，那家店免费给了我们纸。到六月，新书架满了，旧铁盒也空了。"},"gear":{"tw":[["train",0],["park",3],["wheel",2],["automatic",6],["pitch",0],["reverse",3],["adapt",2],["vehicle",6]],"en":"My first driving lesson was in a wide car park behind the station, where a train passed every ten minutes. The old vehicle had a heavy wheel and no automatic gear, so I had to learn to change every one by hand. We would pitch forward and stop, then reverse, then try again. My teacher told me to adapt my feet to the pedals before I touched the road. By the third lesson I could hold the car steady on a slope. He said the rest was only practice. It took me a year to feel easy on the road.","zh":"我的第一节驾驶课在车站后面一个大停车场里，那儿每十分钟过一趟火车。那台旧车方向盘很沉，也没有自动挡，每个挡都得我用手换。我们往前一冲就停，再倒回来，再试一遍。教练让我先让脚在踏板上适应好，再上路。到第三节课，我已经能让车子稳稳停在坡上了。他说，剩下的只是练。我花了一年才在路上开得轻松。"},"grant":{"tw":[["allow",0],["pension",3],["agree",2],["return",6],["award",3],["general",2],["receive",6],["yield",0]],"en":"The committee would not grant a penny without a written plan. They had to allow us two weeks to prepare, and in the end they agreed to our figures. It was not a large award, but with my father's small pension it was enough to begin. The general view in the village was that we should not receive more than we needed. In return, we promised to keep the accounts open to everyone. A year later the old hall began to yield real money for the school. Nobody has asked for a second grant since, and I think that says something.","zh":"委员会不见书面方案，一分钱也不肯拨。他们答应给我们两周时间准备，最后认可了我们的数字。这笔奖励不算多，但加上我爸那点养老金，够开工了。村里普遍的看法是，我们该拿的不该超过我们真正需要的。作为回报，我们答应把账目对所有人公开。一年之后，那座旧礼堂开始给学校带来实实在在的收入。从那以后，没人再申请第二笔拨款——我想这本身就说明了点什么。"},"hedge":{"tw":[["duck",0],["quibble",3],["avoid",2],["mortgage",6],["skirt",0],["fence",2],["bond",6],["dodge",0]],"en":"On Sunday my uncle would stand in the garden and trim the hedge by the fence, and while he worked he worried about the mortgage. He was not the kind of man to quibble over small sums, but he did know how to dodge a bad deal. He would duck the questions of any neighbour who wanted to borrow money, and skirt the subject of the bond he had bought. It was his way of avoiding trouble, and it cost him nothing. The hedge always came out straight. I never once saw him lose his temper over any of it.","zh":"星期天我叔叔总在园子里修剪篱笆墙边的树篱，一边干活一边愁着房贷。他不是那种为小钱计较的人，可他懂得怎么躲开吃亏的买卖。邻居来借钱，他就绕开话头；他买的那笔债券，他也避而不谈。那是他躲麻烦的法子，一点不费什么。他剪出来的树篱总是笔直的。这些事，我从没见他动过一次气。"},"height":{"tw":[["top",0],["ceiling",3],["degree",2],["length",6],["peak",0],["highness",3],["tall",6],["summit",0]],"en":"For our science project we had to measure the height of the water tower on the hill. We wrote down the length of its shadow and the angle in degrees, then worked out the top by drawing. Nobody could agree on the true summit, and two figures were quite close. The teacher said that at its peak the tower was taller than any building in the town. We talked about the highness of the clouds above it, and about the low ceiling of grey that followed. It rained before we finished, and our paper went soft. The number we kept was only a little wrong.","zh":"科学课上我们要量山上那座水塔的高度。我们记下影子的长度和角度数，再靠画图求出顶端。真正的高度谁也对不上，两个数倒很接近。老师说，这座塔最高的时候比镇上任何一栋楼都高。我们还聊到塔上方云层的高度，以及随后压下来的那片灰蒙蒙的低云。我们还没做完就下雨了，纸都泡软了。我们最后留下的那个数，只错了一点点。"},"individual":{"tw":[["single",0],["head",3],["common",1],["equal",6],["private",0],["creature",3],["represent",6],["soul",0]],"en":"The school asked every individual in the village to write down a few lines about their own life. Not one single person refused, though some wanted their name kept private. The head of the group said it did not matter whether we were rich or poor; each account was of equal worth. It was a common idea, but it worked. A shy old man wrote that he was only a small creature in a big world, and that his own soul had never seemed worth describing. His page was read aloud to everyone. Someone said it seemed to represent the whole street.","zh":"学校请村里每个人写下几行自己的日子。没有一个人拒绝，虽然有人希望名字不要公开。小组的负责人说，穷也好富也好，都不相干；每一篇分量都一样。这道理很普通，却真管用。一位不爱说话的老人写道，他不过是大世界里一个小小的生灵，他自己那点心思从来不值得写下来。他那一页被念给了所有人听。有人说，那一页像是把整条街都写进去了。"},"injure":{"tw":[["hurt",2],["shoot",3],["damage",2],["maim",6],["wound",0],["harm",3],["incapacitate",6],["bruise",0]],"en":"On the last bend of the race, a young rider fell and seemed to injure his shoulder badly. The fall did not shoot him off the road, but it did damage the front wheel of his machine. A bad wound on his arm began to bruise within minutes, and his coach feared it might maim his hand for months. He was helped up at once, and the doctor said the injury would not harm his chances next year. It could incapacitate him for a few weeks, nothing more. He said it hurt more than he let us see. He was back on a bike by the spring.","zh":"比赛最后一个弯道上，一个年轻骑手摔了，肩膀伤得不轻。这一摔没把他甩出路面，却撞坏了车子的前轮。胳膊上那道伤口几分钟内就青肿起来，教练怕他这只手几个月都用不了。大家马上把他扶起来，医生说这伤不会影响他明年的机会，最多让他歇上几周。他说，其实疼得比他让我们看出来的厉害。到了春天，他又骑上车了。"},"instance":{"tw":[["example",0],["piece",3],["elaborate",2],["same",6],["illustrate",0],["exception",3],["similar",6],["exemplify",0]],"en":"The teacher asked for one instance where the rule did not work, and for a moment nobody spoke. Then a girl gave an example from her own street, and it was exactly the same as the one in the book. She offered to illustrate it on the board with a piece of chalk, and the class watched her draw two similar lines. The teacher said this was no exception but a good case, and asked another student to exemplify it in words. He began to elaborate, and the bell rang before he had finished. We wrote it up that evening.","zh":"老师让大家举一个这条规则不成立的例子，一时间没人作声。后来一个女生举了她家那条街上的例子，恰好跟书上的那一个一模一样。她说要用一支粉笔在黑板上画出来，全班看着她画了两条相似的线。老师说这不是例外，而是一个好例子，又叫另一个学生用话把它说明白。他刚展开讲，下课铃就响了。那天晚上我们把它整理成了笔记。"},"dare":{"tw":[["presume",0],["brazen",3],["act",2],["bother",6],["defy",0],["challenge",2],["tell",6]],"en":"My little brother was the only one in the class who would dare to ask the teacher why. The brazen ones sat at the back and never said a word, but he would act on every question that came to him. He did not mean to defy anyone; he simply could not bother to pretend. Once he stood up and told the head teacher that a rule made no sense. That was a challenge nobody had ever accepted before. I presume he was afraid inside, but it never showed on his face. The teacher, after a long pause, changed the rule.","zh":"我小弟是班里唯一敢问老师为什么的人。那些胆大包天的都坐在后排，一句话也不说，而他一有疑问就去问。他并不是想跟谁对着干，他只是懒得装。有一次他站起来，跟校长说有条规矩根本讲不通。那是一个从来没人敢接的挑战。我猜他心里其实也怕，但脸上一点都看不出来。老师沉默了好一会儿，把那条规矩改了。"},"deny":{"tw":[["refuse",0],["repudiate",3],["admit",1],["accept",6],["traverse",0],["disclaim",3],["acknowledge",6]],"en":"The company first tried to deny that the machine had failed, then had to admit it was true. A spokesman would refuse to answer any question about the cost, and the office seemed ready to repudiate the whole report. In the end the manager had to accept the facts and acknowledge the fault in writing. He also had to traverse the long story of how the fault began, step by step, for the committee. They had wanted to disclaim all responsibility, but nothing could be hidden for long. The repair took three weeks. Nobody in the office ever spoke of it again.","zh":"公司一开始想否认机器出过故障，后来又不得不承认确有其事。一位发言人拒绝对费用的问题作答，办公室似乎也准备把整份报告一笔否掉。最后经理只好接受事实，并书面承认了过失。他还得为委员会把故障是怎么一步步发生的经过从头讲一遍。他们本想撇清一切责任，可什么都藏不了多久。修理花了三个星期。办公室里再没人提过这件事。"},"detect":{"tw":[["discover",0],["see",3],["spy",2],["simulate",6],["find",0],["sense",3],["transmit",6]],"en":"The small machine was built to detect the faintest change in the air. It could see a rise in dust long before any of us could sense it. Engineers would simulate a storm in the lab to test how fast it could find a fault, and then transmit the result to a screen upstairs. Once, it caught something none of us could spy with our own eyes. They said the real point was not to discover the fault itself, but to find it early. That one test saved the whole station. After that night, nobody questioned the little box again.","zh":"那台小机器是用来探测空气里最细微的变化的。它能在我们任何人感觉到之前，就先看见尘埃升高。工程师会在实验室里模拟一场风暴，测它多快能找到故障，再把结果传到楼上的屏幕上。有一次，它抓住了我们用眼睛谁也看不见的东西。他们说，真正的发现不是那个故障本身，而是它被发现得有多早。那一次测试救了整个站。那晚之后，再没人质疑过那个小箱子。"},"disturb":{"tw":[["touch",0],["toss",3],["interfere",6],["trouble",0],["violate",3],["disrupt",6],["interrupt",0]],"en":"The reading room was so quiet that even a turning page could disturb the man at the far desk. He would touch his glasses and look up, but he never said a word. A student who wanted to toss a note across the table was told not to interfere with the others. The librarian said noise would disrupt the whole room, and that a single loud word could interrupt an hour of work. Nobody wanted to trouble her, so everyone kept still. But one rule said no food, and someone had brought a whole lunch in. That seemed to violate more than any whisper.","zh":"阅览室里安静到连翻一页纸都可能打扰到最里头那位先生。他会扶一下眼镜抬起头，却从不说话。有个学生想隔着桌子扔张纸条，被告知不要妨碍别人。图书管理员说，响声会搅乱整间屋子，一个响亮的字就能打断一小时的工作。谁也不想给她添麻烦，于是大家都静静的。可有一条规矩写着不许带吃的，偏偏有人把一整份午饭带了进来。那件事，似乎比任何窃窃私语都更出格。"},"dive":{"tw":[["plunge",0],["duck",3],["swim",2],["boat",6],["flip",3],["descend",2],["balloon",6]],"en":"On the hottest day of summer we took the boat out to the middle of the lake. My brother would plunge in first, then dive again and again from the low rail. A duck would swim past us without any fear, and once a lost balloon came down from the sky and drifted onto the water. My sister liked to flip backward off the edge, which always made the old boat rock. As the sun began to descend, the water turned cold and nobody wanted to get back in. We rowed home slowly, still wet. It was the best afternoon of that whole summer.","zh":"夏天最热的那天，我们把船划到了湖心。我弟先一头扎进水里，然后从低矮的船舷上一遍遍往下跳。一只鸭子不怕生地游过我们身边，还有一只飘丢的气球从天上落下来，漂在水面上。我姐喜欢从船边向后翻下去，每次都把那条旧船晃得直摇。太阳开始往下沉时，水变凉了，谁也不想再下去。我们慢慢把船划回家，身上还是湿的。那是整个夏天最好的一个下午。"},"drag":{"tw":[["draw",0],["move",2],["slow",6],["pull",2],["travel",2],["trigger",6],["cart",0]],"en":"The old cart had to be dragged up the hill, and it was slow work. My grandfather would draw the rope over his shoulder and pull with his whole body. Two of us would push behind, and the wheels would move an inch at a time. He said a heavy load would drag down even the strongest man, and that the trick was never to stop. They would travel that same road every autumn, with the harvest piled high. Once a loose stone was enough to trigger the whole thing rolling back. Nobody was hurt, but we never forgot it.","zh":"那辆旧板车得拖上山，这活儿很慢。我爷爷会把绳子搭到肩上，用整个身子去拉。我们两个人从后面推，轮子一次只挪一寸。他说重载能把最强壮的人拖垮，诀窍就是别停下。每年秋天他们都走同一条路，车上堆满了收成。有一次，一块松动的石头就足以让整辆车往回溜。好在没人受伤，可我们一直记着那回。"},"drum":{"tw":[["beat",0],["play",2],["percussion",6],["bone",0],["sound",2],["trumpet",6],["barrel",0]],"en":"At the village festival a man would play the drum with both hands, and the sound carried all the way down the street. He had made the barrel shell himself and stretched an old skin over it, and beside him another player blew a long trumpet. He would beat a slow rhythm first, then move into a faster one, and the children danced. A bone from some animal hung on the side as a lucky charm. He said the drum was the oldest kind of percussion, older than any horn. Nobody could stand still when he started. We heard it from three streets away.","zh":"村里的节庆上，一个男人用双手敲鼓，鼓声一直传到街那头。鼓身是他自己做的木桶，上面蒙了一张旧皮，旁边另一个乐手吹着一支长号。他先敲一段慢的，再转成快的，孩子们就跳起来。一侧还挂着一根兽骨，算是求个吉利。他说鼓是最古老的打击乐，比任何号角都早。他一敲起来，谁都没法站着不动。我们隔着三条街就听见了。"},"dump":{"tw":[["floor",0],["beat",2],["garbage",6],["deck",0],["drop",2],["waste",6],["plunge",0]],"en":"On the last day of the holiday we had to dump everything we no longer needed. Old chairs sat on the floor by the door, and a pile of garbage grew on the deck outside. My father would beat the dust out of the mats and drop the broken ones into a bag. It seemed a waste to throw out things that still worked, so we gave some away. Once he slipped on the wet deck and nearly took a plunge into the water below. We laughed about it later, over a cup of tea. The house felt lighter by the evening.","zh":"假期的最后一天，我们得把不再需要的东西都扔出去。旧椅子摆在门口的地板上，外面甲板上垃圾堆了一堆。我爸会把垫子上的灰拍出来，把破的丢进袋里。还能用的东西扔掉太可惜，所以我们送出了一些。有一次他在湿甲板上滑了一下，差点一头栽进下面的水里。后来我们喝着茶，把这事当笑话说。到晚上，屋子显得轻快多了。"},"encourage":{"tw":[["further",0],["carry",3],["support",2],["discourage",1],["aim",6],["help",3],["inspire",2]],"en":"Her teacher would encourage every student to read one more book each month, and would never discourage even the slowest one. She would carry a box of stories to class and let anyone borrow from it. Her aim was simple: to make reading a habit, not a task. When a girl said she could not finish, the teacher would help her choose something shorter, support her choice, and inspire her to try again. Parents were told not to push further than the child could go. Half the class kept reading long after the year ended. Twenty years later, some of them still write to her.","zh":"她的老师会鼓励每个学生每月多读一本书，连最慢的那个也不打击。她会抱一箱故事书来上课，谁都可以借。她的目标很简单：让读书变成习惯，而不是任务。有个女孩说自己读不完，老师就帮她挑一本短些的，支持她的选择，再激励她重新试一次。家长也被叮嘱，别逼得超过孩子能承受的程度。那一年过去很久了，班里一半的人还在读。二十年后，其中还有几个给她写信。"},"energy":{"tw":[["zip",0],["juice",3],["drive",2],["gas",6],["vitality",3],["force",2],["petroleum",6]],"en":"After a long illness my father had no energy left, and for a while he could not even climb the stairs. My mother would give him a glass of fresh juice each morning and urge him to walk a little. She said vitality comes back slowly, like a car running low on gas. He had always been the one with the zip and the drive to fix anything in the house. Now the smallest task took all his force. In the end he gave up the old car that ran on petroleum and bought a slow bicycle instead. It was the right choice.","zh":"一场大病之后，我爸一点精力都没有了，有一阵连楼梯都上不去。我妈每天早上给他一杯鲜果汁，催他走几步。她说元气是慢慢回来的，就像一辆快没油的车。从前家里但凡有什么要修的，都是他有那股劲头、那份干劲。如今最小的一件事也要耗尽他所有的力气。最后他放弃了那辆烧汽油的旧车，换了一辆慢悠悠的自行车。这个选择是对的。"},"estate":{"tw":[["land",0],["entail",3],["class",2],["condominium",6],["homestead",3],["property",2],["fortune",6]],"en":"When my grandfather died, the estate was smaller than anyone expected. There was the land behind the house, a small homestead, and one old condominium in the city. To divide it all fairly would entail weeks of work, and every class of relative had an opinion. My mother said a property is more than its price, and that a fortune can vanish in a single bad year. In the end they sold nothing and kept the land in the family. The house still stands, though the fence is gone. Nobody in the family ever talked about money again. That quiet choice kept us together for years.","zh":"我爷爷去世时，留下的产业比谁想的都小。屋后有一块地，一处小小的宅院，还有城里一套旧公寓。要公平地分开，得花上好几个星期，而哪一房亲戚都有话说。我妈说，一份家业不只是它的价钱，一笔财富也可能在一年里就没了。最后他们什么也没卖，把地留在了家里。房子还立着，只是篱笆没了。家里再没人提过钱的事。那个安静的决定，把我们拢在一起好多年。"},"exercise":{"tw":[["use",2],["play",3],["conduct",6],["work",2],["train",3],["effective",6],["practise",0]],"en":"My doctor told me I had to exercise every day, not just now and then. He said the use of a gym was not much help unless I made it a habit. So I began to work at it in the morning, and to train with a small group at the weekend. We would play a short game first, then conduct a set of slow movements together. It was effective only after a few months, and even then it was easy to give up. He said the trick is to practise a little, often, rather than a lot, once. I still keep to that plan today.","zh":"医生跟我说，我得每天锻炼，不能三天打鱼两天晒网。他说，就算办了健身卡，不养成习惯也没多大用。于是我早上开始坚持练，周末还跟一个小队一起训练。我们通常先打一场短球，再一起做一套慢动作。这套东西得过几个月才见效，而且就算见效了，也很容易放弃。他说诀窍就是少练、常练，而不是一次练很多。我到今天还照这个计划做着。"},"expose":{"tw":[["discover",0],["spring",3],["subject",2],["pose",6],["display",0],["distract",6],["exhibit",0]],"en":"The young photographer wanted to expose a side of the town that no one ever showed. Her first exhibit was held in a small room in spring, and every picture displayed the faces of people at work. She would pose her subjects only lightly, because she did not want to distract them from what they were doing. Some said the work might discover a truth the town preferred to hide. Others thought such a display was too close to the bone. But the room was full every evening, and nobody left early. She called it a mirror, not a window, and left the room to the visitors.","zh":"那位年轻摄影师想拍出这座小镇从没人展示过的一面。她的第一次展览办在春天的一间小屋里，每张照片都是干活的人的脸。她只让对方轻轻摆一点姿势，因为她不想让他们从手头的事上分心。有人说这组作品也许能显露出小镇宁可藏起来的真相；也有人觉得这样的展示太戳人了。可每到晚上屋里都挤满人，谁也没提前走。她说这是一面镜子，不是一扇窗，然后把屋子留给了参观的人。"},"feather":{"tw":[["square",0],["cover",2],["goose",6],["plume",0],["grow",2],["bald",6],["fledge",0]],"en":"A grey goose had built its nest in the square patch of grass behind the shed. My mother would cover the spot with a net so the cat would stay away. Each feather was soft to the touch, and a single plume would drift onto the path and stay there for days. The young birds began to grow fast, and by June the last one was ready to fledge from the nest. A bald patch of ground was all that was left. She said the whole garden had waited for that one morning. She still watches for the same nest each spring.","zh":"一只灰鹅在棚子后那一小方块草地上筑了窝。我妈用一张网把那地方罩起来，免得猫过来。每根羽毛摸上去都软软的，一根绒毛飘到小路上，能在那儿待好几天。小鸟长得很快，到六月最后一只也快要离巢了。最后只剩下一小块光秃秃的地。她说，整个花园都在等那个早晨。每年春天，她还在留意同一个窝。"},"flame":{"tw":[["fire",0],["blaze",3],["burn",2],["torch",6],["flare",3],["shine",2],["candle",6]],"en":"When the power went out that night, we lit a single candle and its flame threw long shadows on the wall. My grandmother held a small torch above the table, and its light made the room shine for a moment. Someone said a fire had started in a field outside town, a blaze that could be seen for miles. We could only watch from the window as the sky seemed to burn red at the edge. Then the lights came back, and the small flare in the glass looked suddenly pale and useless. She blew it out and went to bed.","zh":"那天晚上停电后，我们点了一根蜡烛，火苗在墙上投下长长的影子。奶奶在桌上举着一只小手电，那一小片光照得屋里亮了一瞬。有人说镇外的田里起了火，那火光几里外都能看见。我们只能从窗口望着，天边像是烧红了一样。后来灯又亮了，杯子里那点微光顿时显得又白又没用。她把蜡烛吹灭，去睡了。"},"fortune":{"tw":[["lot",0],["misfortune",3],["treasure",2],["money",6],["luck",0],["wealth",6],["fate",0]],"en":"My uncle never had much money, but he always said he had had a lot of luck. When the factory closed, it seemed a real misfortune, and for a year he had no work at all. Still, he would tell us that wealth is not measured only in coins. He found a small treasure in an old box his father had left, a watch with a broken face, and he wore it every day. He said fate gives everyone one good year, and you should not waste it. In his case that year came late, but it came. He called it his fortune and meant it.","zh":"我叔一辈子没什么钱，却总说自己运气很好。厂子关门那阵，看着是场大不幸，他整整一年没活干。可他还是会跟我们说，财富不只用钱来算。他在父亲留下的一个旧箱子里找到一件小宝贝——一只表盘破了的怀表，他天天戴着。他说，命运给每个人都留了一个好年头，别把它浪费掉。他这一例来得晚，可到底来了。他管那叫他的福气，而且是认真的。"},"frost":{"tw":[["freeze",2],["cover",2],["brown",6],["ice",2],["damage",2],["leach",6],["icing",0]],"en":"That October the first frost came early, and by morning the whole field was white. The cold would freeze the top of the ground and cover every leaf with a thin layer of ice. My father knew it could damage the last of the crop before we could bring it in. He said the rain had already begun to leach the good out of the soil, and now this. In the kitchen my mother was making icing for a small cake, and the brown sugar sat beside her. She said the garden would look sad for a week, then forget all about it.","zh":"那年十月头一场霜来得早，到早上整片地都白了。寒气冻住地表，给每片叶子都盖上一层薄冰。我爸知道，还没等我们把最后那点庄稼收回来，它就可能被冻坏。他说雨水本就已经把地里的养分冲走了，现在又来这么一下。厨房里，我妈在给一个小蛋糕做糖霜，红糖就搁在她旁边。她说花园会难看上一个星期，然后就把这事忘得干干净净。"},"frustrate":{"tw":[["cross",0],["ruin",3],["thwart",6],["spoil",0],["tease",3],["capitalise",6],["foil",0]],"en":"The rain came on the very morning of the village fair, and it seemed to frustrate every plan we had made. A single wet day could ruin the whole work of a month. My father tried to thwart the weather by moving everything into the hall, but the wind still found a way in. The children would tease each other about it and then laugh. We did not want to spoil the day, so we went ahead anyway. Some traders tried to capitalise on the crowd and raised their prices, but one neighbour was firm enough to foil that plan. It turned out well in the end. Nobody stayed cross for long.","zh":"村集那天一早下起了雨，好像把我们所有的打算都打乱了。一个雨天就能毁掉一整个月的活。我爸想把天气挡在门外，把东西全搬进了礼堂，可风还是钻了进来。孩子们拿这事互相打趣，然后笑成一团。我们不想扫了这天的兴，还是照办了。有些商贩想借人多抬价，一个邻居态度一硬，那主意就黄了。结果这天还挺好。没人气恼太久。"},"future":{"tw":[["next",0],["tomorrow",3],["tense",2],["past",1],["change",6],["hereafter",0],["possible",6]],"en":"My cousin sat at the kitchen table and talked about his future for an hour. He said the next few months would decide everything, and that he could not sleep for thinking about tomorrow. The whole room felt tense, because his past had not been easy and he did not want to repeat it. My aunt said one change was possible for anyone, at any age. She told him to stop wondering what would happen hereafter and start with the week in front of him. He smiled then, for the first time that evening. It was a small start, but it was a start.","zh":"我表弟坐在厨房桌边，谈了一个钟头他的未来。他说接下来这几个月会决定一切，一想到明天就睡不着。整间屋子都绷着，因为他过去过得不容易，他不想再重来一遍。我姑说，不管多大年纪，谁都有可能改变。她让他别再琢磨以后会怎样，先从眼前这个星期做起。他这才笑了，那是那天晚上第一次笑。这只是个小开始，可到底是个开始。"},"gift":{"tw":[["present",3],["cover",3],["worth",6],["invest",0],["treat",3],["stamp",6],["talent",0]],"en":"For my sister's birthday I wanted to give her a gift that was really worth something, not just a small present from a shop. I had to cover the cost myself, so I did extra work for weeks and put what I saved into a small fund. My mother said it was foolish to invest so much in one day. But my sister has a talent for painting, and I bought her a set of brushes, a few old stamps, and a box of paints. We shared a quiet treat that evening, and she smiled in a way I still remember.","zh":"姐姐生日那天，我想送她一份真正有价值的东西，而不是商店里随手买的小礼物。钱得我自己出，于是我加了好几周的班，把攒下的钱存进了一个小账户。我妈说为一天花这么多钱太傻。可姐姐有画画的天赋，我给她买了一套笔、几张旧邮票和一盒颜料。那天晚上我们安静地一起吃了点好东西，她笑起来的样子我到现在还记得。"},"instant":{"tw":[["minute",0],["climax",3],["content",6],["moment",2],["pinpoint",3],["touch",6],["second",0]],"en":"For one instant the whole room went quiet, and in that moment I knew the answer was wrong. I had worked on the report for weeks, checking every minute detail, and this was the second time a small error had slipped through. My boss could pinpoint the fault at a single touch. The climax came when she asked me to read the content aloud. I felt the floor move under my feet. For a moment nobody spoke, and then she said we would fix it together in the morning. I did not sleep much that night, and the fault was mine.","zh":"有那么一瞬，整个房间静了下来，就在那一刻我知道答案错了。这份报告我做了好几周，连每一分钟的细节都核对过，而这已经是第二次让一个小错溜过去。老板一碰就能指出毛病在哪儿。最紧张的一刻是她让我把内容念出来的时候。我觉得脚下的地板都在动。那片刻谁也没出声，然后她说，明早我们一起改。那天晚上我没怎么睡，错在我。"},"instruct":{"tw":[["teach",0],["charge",3],["inform",2],["advise",6],["coach",3],["order",2],["consult",6]],"en":"The head coach had to instruct a group of new teachers before the term began. He would teach them how to keep a class quiet and when to consult an older colleague. He told them to inform parents early if a child was in trouble, and never to charge for the extra help they gave. His first order was simple: never shame a student in front of others. I had come to advise him on the new rules, but I stayed and listened instead. By the end I felt I had learned as much as the teachers.","zh":"开学前，主教练得给一群新老师做指导。他会教他们怎么让课堂安静下来，什么时候去请教老同事。他让他们在孩子出问题时尽早通知家长，还要求额外补课不许收费。他下的第一道命令很简单：绝不当着别人的面羞辱学生。我本来只是去给他讲新规定的，结果留下来听着。到结束时，我觉得自己学到的东西跟那些老师一样多。"},"introduce":{"tw":[["enter",0],["feed",3],["adopt",6],["present",3],["slip",3],["use",6],["insert",0]],"en":"When I first had to introduce the new system to the staff, my hands were shaking. I would enter the room, present each step, and then let them use it on their own. It was easy to insert the wrong number and slip into the wrong file. The factory had decided to adopt the whole thing at once, which made it worse. My job was also to feed the old records into the machine, one page at a time. A woman near the door raised her hand and asked whether we could go slower. We did not finish until after dark.","zh":"第一次要把这套新系统介绍给同事时，我的手一直在抖。我会先走进房间，一步步演示，然后让他们自己动手用。输错一个数字、滑进另一个文件太容易了。厂里决定一下子全部改用这套东西，这让事情更难。我的活儿还得把旧记录一页页喂进机器里。门边一个女人举手问，能不能慢一点。我们一直弄到天黑才结束。"},"item":{"tw":[["particular",0],["highlight",3],["symbol",2],["copy",6],["detail",0],["menu",6],["token",0]],"en":"On the menu that night one item caught my eye. It was not the highlight of the page, just a small line with a strange symbol beside it. I asked the waiter for a copy of the list so I could check every detail. He said one particular dish had run out, and he offered me a token for a free drink instead. I read the whole thing twice and still could not decide. In the end I ordered the cheapest thing on the page and ate it slowly. My friend had already finished and was waiting by the door.","zh":"那天晚上菜单上有一样东西引起了我的注意。它不是那一页上最显眼的一道，只是小小一行，旁边有个奇怪的符号。我向服务员要了一份单子，好把每个细节都看清楚。他说有一道特别的菜卖完了，作为补偿给了我一张免费饮料的券。我把整页读了两遍还是拿不定主意。最后我点了这一页上最便宜的一样，慢慢吃完。朋友早就吃完了，在门口等着。"},"knife":{"tw":[["tongue",0],["dagger",3],["injure",2],["nail",6],["stab",0],["weapon",2],["wound",6]],"en":"The knife slipped while my father was cutting bread, and the wound in his hand would not stop bleeding. He had used the same blade for years and never thought of it as a weapon. Each time he moved his fingers the pain came back like a stab. My mother cleaned the cut and told him to hold his tongue, because he kept saying it was nothing. A small dagger hung on the wall, a gift from his brother, and a bent nail was above the door. At the clinic they closed the wound, and I told him not to injure himself again.","zh":"我爸切面包时刀滑了，手上的伤口止不住地流血。那把刀他用了好多年，从没把它当成凶器。每次他动一下手指，疼得就像被扎了一刀。我妈给他清洗伤口，叫他别说话，因为他老说没事。墙上挂着一把小匕首，是他弟弟送的，门上方还有一颗弯了的钉子。到了诊室他们把伤口缝上了，我跟他说，别再把自己弄伤了。"}}});
